    "synthesis": "# Index Entry-Creation Plans — Adversarial Synthesis\n\n**Scope:** all entry-creation planning documents in `plans/` (plus `tmp/Dissertation/DISSERTATION-ANALYSIS-PIPELINE-PLAN.md`), judged against the 27 built entries, 1,758 files, and 551 audit defects.\n**Purpose:** direct input to a NEW claim/clause-level entry-creation plan.\n\n**Plan-file shorthand used throughout:**\n\n| Tag | File |\n|---|---|\n| `TEMPLATE` | `plans/secondary-cluster-index-plan-TEMPLATE-2026-07-15.md` (238 lines) |\n| `BOR-SEC` | `plans/boredom-secondary-cluster-index-plan-2026-07-14.md` (287 lines) |\n| `VR-PED` | `plans/vr-pedagogy-secondary-cluster-index-plan-2026-07-15.md` (244 lines) |\n| `BEX-v1 / BEX-v2 / BEX-ANCHOR` | `plans/boredom-experiment-index-entry-plan-2026-07-10.md` / `-v2-2026-07-11.md` / `plans/boredom-experiment-channel-schema-anchor-plan-2026-07-16.md` |\n| `NEWMEDIA` | `plans/new-media-presence-ingestion-phase1-report-2026-07-20.md` |\n| `USAGE` | `plans/corpus-index-usage-plan.md` |\n| `MIGRATION` / `COMPARE` / `EVAL` | `plans/archon-corpus-index-migration-spec.md` / `-comparison-report.md` / `plans/index-system-ab-c-evaluation-plan.md` |\n| `WENDT` | `plans/wendt-design-for-dasein-analysis.md` |\n| `DISS-PIPE` | `tmp/Dissertation/DISSERTATION-ANALYSIS-PIPELINE-PLAN.md` |\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the current authoring process actually is\n\n### 1.1 The pipeline as practised\n\nThe canonical process is `TEMPLATE`, a \"fill §P, then a cheaper model (Sonnet) executes Phases −1 → 5\" procedure (`TEMPLATE:7`). It has six phases, two human gates, and a source-linear agent budget.\n\n**§P — Parameters (`TEMPLATE:15-27`).** Seven hand-filled values: `SOURCE_DIR`, `CLUSTER_NAME`, `PREFIX`, `PURPOSE`, `ANCHORS` (0–2 existing entries), `ANCHOR_EDGE_NAMES`, `CONCORDANCE_HINT`. This is declared \"the ONLY hand-authored part.\" Everything below is asserted invariant.\n\n**§0 — Anchor + provenance + copyright discipline (`TEMPLATE:30-45`).** Three rules that carry through every artifact: bridge-never-duplicate to anchor entries; a three-value provenance vocabulary `FE` / `FAITHFUL-<AUTHOR>` / `P·anticipatory-application`; and a blanket \"**No ≥25-word verbatim quotation anywhere**\" with ≤12-word anchor phrases (`TEMPLATE:44-45`).\n\n**Phase −1 — Survey & self-authored spec (`TEMPLATE:47-98`).** `pdfinfo` + `md5sum` + `pdftotext -l 3` inventory (`:54`); de-dup/haystack rubric (`:57-67`); strand assignment, 4–8 strands, merge strands with <3 members (`:68-70`); id assignment `<PREFIX>NN` with `-00-` reserved for a corpus overview (`:73`); depth rubric map/deep/deep-long by page count (`:76-77`); concordance-axis derivation, ≤15 rows × ≤15 columns (`:81-88`); object-type vocabulary ≤12 (`:90-98`).\n\n**GATE G0 (`TEMPLATE:100-103`).** The filled cluster-specific spec is written to `plans/` and execution **stops** for user sign-off.\n\n**Phase 0 — extraction + overview (`TEMPLATE:137-148`).** `pdftotext` every source to the **scratchpad**, one `.txt` per source; agents receive the `.txt` path, never the PDF; near-empty output flagged `OCR-LOW`. Emit `phase0-overview.md` and `_synthesis/manifest.json` with the fixed key list at `:145-148`.\n\n**Phase 1 — per-source metadata (`TEMPLATE:149-151`).** One agent per unit, batched ~8, writing header-only JSON.\n\n**Phase 2 — deep per-source (`TEMPLATE:152-165`).** One agent per unit (two-pass for `deep-long`). Each emits a **trio**:\n- `<PREFIX>NN-<slug>.md`, budgeted in **words** (1,500–3,500 humanities / 1,000–2,500 empirical / 400–1,000 map, `:154-155`), following a fixed 9-part narrative skeleton ending in a \"Not treated:\" line (`:156-158`);\n- `<PREFIX>NN-<slug>.json`, specified as a **bare list of key names** — `constructs[], measures[], readings[], concepts[], interlocutors[], tensions[], bridges{}` (`:159-161`);\n- `<PREFIX>NN-<slug>-edges.csv`, columns `source,relation,target,locus,note`, edge floors 12/20/35 (`:162-165`).\n\n**Phase 3 — cluster synthesis, main loop only (`TEMPLATE:167-181`).** 3A ontology (`#### N. Name` header format, \"Replicate the Boredom/FCM structure exactly\", `:168-172`); 3B `global-edges.csv` \"concat + dedup\" + debate map (`:173`); 3C concept matrix + contested readings; 3D concordance + terminology appendix; 3E citation networks + 5 Mermaid graphs + scholarly-evolution narrative.\n\n**Phase 4 — cross-pipeline bridge (`TEMPLATE:182-185`).** `bridge-sources/anchor-pointers.md` + one `.mmd`, hard-capped ≤25 edges.\n\n**Phase 5 — compiler wiring (`TEMPLATE:187-201`).** Backup, hand-edit one dict entry into `TEXT_DIRS` in `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py`, run it, \"verify node/term counts by reading\", \"re-run the repo's verbatim-quote detector.\"\n\n**GATE G1 (`TEMPLATE:200-201`).** Show the `TEXT_DIRS` diff + compiled counts + one sample unit trio, wait for sign-off, never commit before G1.\n\n**§8 gates (`TEMPLATE:216-229`).** Fourteen markdown checkboxes. Verified in place: the section header is at `:215` and the checkbox block runs `:217-229`.\n\n**§7 orchestration (`TEMPLATE:205-214`).** Agent tool, not Workflow. Budget `1 + N + N`. Documented reliability lesson: pre/post-task hooks no-op a subagent ~1 in 8; mitigation is \"verify all three files exist on disk for every unit and **self-author any gaps**\" (`:208-210`). Deviations recorded in `manifest.json → planCorrections` (`:214`).\n\n### 1.2 The three other plan lineages actually in use\n\n- **Hand-written cluster plans** (`BOR-SEC`, `VR-PED`) — same shape but with the vocabulary hand-authored inline. `BOR-SEC` is the template's declared parent (`TEMPLATE:4`).\n- **Single-entry/anchor plans** (`BEX-v1`, `BEX-v2`, `BEX-ANCHOR`) — 795 lines across three versions, producing a 9-file, 7-node entry. `BEX-ANCHOR:96` explicitly redefines the deliverable as \"the node itself + its outbound edges.\"\n- **A phase report used as a creation plan** (`NEWMEDIA`) — no gates section, no acceptance criteria, one quality clause at `:135`. It produced three entries (Presence Theory, Social Presence, Rhetoric of Interactivity: 10 / 8 / 7 files).\n\n### 1.3 Cost profile of one entry\n\nMeasured from the two best-documented builds:\n\n| | Boredom Secondary (N=55) | VR Pedagogy Secondary (N=34) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Agent invocations | ~1 + 55 + 55 = **111** | ~1 + 34 + 34 = **69** (plan budgeted 23+23, `VR-PED:209`) |\n| Wall-clock | 2026-07-14 18:xx → 21:19 + follow-ups | 2026-07-15 → 07-16 + a 07-16 correction pass |\n| Files produced | 189 | 127 |\n| Authored prose | 137,928 words of unit analysis | 99,531 words |\n| Structured sub-items | 2,924 across 55 unit JSONs | ~1,300 records |\n| Edge rows | 3,815 per-unit → 1,897 global (552 KB CSV) | 2,260 per-unit → 1,129 global (304 KB) |\n| **Records reaching runtime** | **68 ontology nodes (2.3%)** | **60 nodes, 19 of them corrupted (≈1%)** |\n| Gate artifacts emitted | 0 | 0 |\n\nCorpus-wide: 1,758 files / 35.3 MB under `corpus/index/` compile to a 664 KB `compiled-index.json` whose node records carry no id, no page, no quote, no locus. Reference cost for the alternative: the claim-level sandbox extracted **3,776 claims from 15 papers for ~$20** (~$1.33/paper, ~$0.005/claim), and drafting runs cost ~$0.30 each.\n\n**The headline economics:** the current process spends ~111 agent-runs and ~138k words to deliver 68 name-only strings to runtime, at roughly **one addressable record per 1,009 source words**. The two entries that hit the goal (`corpus/index/Dissertation/`, `corpus/index/Veri(dis)similitude (Salvo MA)/`) achieve **one per 58–59 words** and were built **outside every plan in `plans/`** — and neither is registered.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Plan defect register\n\nAll 207 plan defects stand. The verification arm returned **zero rows in both the CONFIRMED and REFUTED channels of this input**, so no plan defect was independently overturned here; the audit's own statement that 89 of 93 spot-verified findings survived refutation applies to the *entry* findings, and the 4 non-survivors are not identified in this input. I independently re-verified five load-bearing code facts before writing (§2.3) and adjudicated six inter-reviewer contradictions (§2.4).\n\n### 2.1 CRITICAL — causal chains\n\n**D01 — The plan commissions ~14 synthesis artifacts and wires 1.**\n`TEMPLATE:107-133` mandates the folder layout; `TEMPLATE:190-197` wires exactly one `TEXT_DIRS` entry with `ontology_format: \"header\"`.\n→ **Code reality (re-verified):** `collect_ontology_nodes` (`compile-corpus-index.py:1217-1229`) opens `book-level-ontology.md`, falling back to `cluster-ontology.md`, and nothing else; `collect_tension_edges` (`:1253-1274`) opens `_synthesis/tension-edges.json`. `grep -c 'edges.csv' scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` = 0.\n→ **Observed:** Boredom Secondary's 2,924 sub-items, 3,815 per-unit edges, 1,897-row `global-edges.csv`, 91 concordance cells, 72 lemmas, 65 citation links and 211 tensions all reach runtime as **zero**. VR Pedagogy: 126 of 127 files unreachable.\n→ **Consequence:** the overwhelming majority of the programme's spend is authored into a void, and the fact is invisible because no gate measures reachability.\n\n**D02 — `tension-edges.json` is the compiler's only edge channel and appears in no plan.**\nThe string \"tension-edges\" appears **0 times** in `TEMPLATE`, 0 times in `BOR-SEC`, 0 times in `VR-PED`, 0 times in the 795 lines of `BEX-*`, 0 times in `NEWMEDIA`. `TEMPLATE:112-124` routes disagreement into `debate-map.{md,json}` and `contested-readings.md` instead.\n→ **Observed:** no template-built cluster has one. `compiled-index.json` holds 64 `tensionEdges`, all from pre-template book entries. Boredom's 165 unit tensions and 12 debate axes contribute 0. Where the file *was* written without a stated schema, 4 of 11 yield zero edges silently (`pole_A/pole_B` — Uncomfortable, 15 lost; `wendt_position/against` — Wendt, 12; label-only — In-Game 12, Grammar 16+21).\n\n**D03 — The atom is the SOURCE, so claim-level output is structurally impossible.**\n`TEMPLATE:127-130` and `:152-165` define one folder / one `.md` / one `.json` / one `-edges.csv` per source keyed `<PREFIX>NN`. `BOR-SEC:203-205` specifies the unit JSON as a bag of parallel arrays. `BOR-SEC:165` lists `READING/CLAIM` as an *edge endpoint category*, never as a record with identity.\n→ **Observed:** 355 unit-record files / ~320 units / 372 unit analyses ≈ 7 records per source against a target of 50–500. Boredom's 463 `readings[]` are addressable by array position only; 296 (63.9%) carry no id.\n\n**D04 — Prose word budgets cap extraction density.**\n`TEMPLATE:154-155` / `BOR-SEC:198-199` / `VR-PED:179` budget the deliverable in **words**; the only quantitative floor per source is an edge count (`TEMPLATE:162-165`).\n→ **Observed:** 18 of 55 Boredom units violate the bands and **17 of the 18 overshoot** — analysts wrote more prose because the JSON had nowhere to put what they found. VR Pedagogy contains ~1,277 provenance-tagged assertions in prose against 233 structured readings (5.5×). Boredom's unit `.md` files contain ~6,300 locus-bearing propositions against 463 structured readings (13.6×).\n\n**D05 — The unit JSON has no element schema; 55 agents invented 42 shapes.**\n`TEMPLATE:159-161` and `BOR-SEC:204` name keys and stop. `BOR-SEC:205` gives a per-field spec for exactly one array (`measures[]`).\n→ **Observed:** `readings[]` in 8 key-signatures; `constructs[]` 5; `measures[]` 7 (including a `sampleN`/`sample_n` case split, 45 vs 38); `concepts[]` 6 including 87 bare strings; `interlocutors[]` 5 including 146 bare strings; `tensions[]` 5 including 46 bare strings; `sections[]` 6 including 57 bare strings. 2,924 sub-items in 42 mutually incompatible shapes. The word \"schema\" appears **0 times** in `TEMPLATE` and **0 times** in `BOR-SEC`; no `*.schema.json` exists anywhere in the repo (verified).\n\n**D06 — No controlled values on any categorical field.**\n`BOR-SEC:165-167` controls object types and edge relations only. No enum for stance, tier, treatment, role, disposition.\n→ **Observed:** `readings[].stance` holds **162 distinct values with 195 nulls**, 108 of them hapax, ranging from `extends` to `\"internal inconsistency (our observation of the source, not a claim it makes about itself)\"`. Worse, **`stance: \"FE\"` appears 22 times** — a provenance tag written into the stance field. The one closed vocabulary that *was* stated (`TEMPLATE:38-42`) leaks too: `FAITHFUL-Elpidorou, p.4` smuggles a locus into the tag.\n\n**D07 — No id grammar below the unit.**\n`BOR-SEC:101-106` specifies ids for the unit only, and does not forbid inventing others.\n→ **Observed:** 9 of 55 agents minted sub-unit ids; `bor-sec-02/-45/-46/-48/-49/-53` all independently minted `C1..C22` and `bor-sec-50/-52` both minted `F1..F8`; **37 values collide, `C1`–`C9` six ways**. The other 46 units left 296 readings permanently unaddressable. Wendt: 91 of 139 claim objects have no id, 20 collide. 4 agents reached the other way and put `§4`, `§2`, `n.8`, `Intro` in the edge CSV **source** column — 119 global rows with a non-id subject.\n\n**D08 — The 25-word verbatim ban makes the target atom unstorable.**\n`TEMPLATE:44-45` and `:225`; `BOR-SEC:199` and `:262`; `VR-PED:31-32`. Applied undifferentiated across the user's own MA thesis, public-domain Aristotle/Equiano/Radcliffe/Austen/Darwin, and third-party monographs.\n→ **Observed:** nothing in 1,758 files carries a sentence offset, character span or bbox. `In-Game .../ig-10-deep.json:434-441` records a `content_filter_audit` retaining definitions only because they are \"24-word … under the 25-word ceiling\", \"23-word … under ceiling\", \"20-word … under ceiling\", and paraphrasing block quotes away. `Uncomfortable .../us-03-radcliffe.json:110,:234` does the same. The threshold is also internally inconsistent — the Uncomfortable plan says 25 at `:178`/`:280` and 30 at `:259`.\n\n**D09 — The named enforcement tool does not exist.**\n`TEMPLATE:198-199`, `:228`; `VR-PED:204`, `:223`; `BEX-ANCHOR:182` all instruct \"re-run the repo's verbatim-quote detector.\"\n→ **Re-verified today:** `scripts/` contains 30 files; the only quote-adjacent one is `substitute-quote-ids.py`, which does something else. The plan's sole automated defence of its central copyright rule is vapour. Compliance is self-reported: RDR2's gates report says \"per-unit agents verified (longest ~19 w).\"\n\n**D10 — \"Compiler runs clean\" is unfalsifiable.**\n`TEMPLATE:227`, `BOR-SEC:239`, `VR-PED:223`, `BEX-v1:261-262`.\n→ **Code reality:** `main()` has no exit-code path and no error accumulator; `parse_header_ontology` (`:513-551`) returns `[]` for an unparsable file **with no warning**, and `collect_ontology_nodes` (verified above) warns only when the file is *missing*. `_normalize_tension_edge` returns `None` on absent `node_a`/`node_b` without warning. A monkey-patched run counted **zero** `warn()` calls while discarding 55 tension records.\n\n**D11 — The 3A heading gate measures a token the parser ignores.**\n`TEMPLATE:227` gates on \"a parseable `## 3A. Canonical Node List`\". For `ontology_format: \"header\"`, `compile-corpus-index.py:533-536` splits the **whole file** on `^#### \\d+\\. ` / `^\\*\\*\\d+\\. `; only `_parse_header_tables` (`:554-566`) restricts to 3A, and only for pipe tables.\n→ **Observed:** Phantasia's `cluster-ontology.md` has 41 identified concept nodes and 22 reading nodes and **0** lines matching `#### N.`; RDR2 Secondary likewise. Registering either yields zero nodes and prints nothing. Conversely any numbered `####` heading anywhere in the file — including narrative prose — silently becomes a global ontology node.\n\n**D12 — \"Replicate the exemplar exactly\" for a machine-parsed file, without stating the field grammar.**\n`TEMPLATE:168-172` / `BOR-SEC:238`. The exemplar (`Boredom .../cluster-ontology.md`) happens to have **zero** parentheticals in its headings, so the advice was safe there. `VR-PED:118-127` then froze its own vocabulary *with* trailing parentheticals — `presence (spatial/physical)`, `immersion (technological)`, `IVR (HMD)`, `conventional instruction (control)` — and `VR-PED:186-187` ordered those labels rendered as `#### N.` headings.\n→ **Code reality:** `_parse_header_section` (`:687-694`) strips an end-anchored parenthetical; `:734-736` assigns it to the node's **`greek`** field whenever no Greek/German lemma exists; `build_canonical_terms` (`:1276-1305`) exports `greek` into the corpus-wide `canonicalTerms` list; `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:268` greedy-matches any term ≥4 chars as a raw substring and applies +0.10 relevance.\n→ **Observed:** 19 of 60 VR Pedagogy nodes corrupted; the bare English words **`technological`** and **`control`** are now live entries in the 1,722-term global greedy-match list, firing on any query against any registered text corpus-wide. Boredom contributed `gaze-based`, `anyone`, `publicness` by the same mechanism. Corpus-wide, **204 of 701 compiled nodes carry an English parenthetical in the `greek` field.**\n\n**D13 — Bridge targets are free text wherever the plan did not enumerate them.**\n`BOR-SEC:24` enumerates FCM target ids literally. `BOR-SEC:170-171` describes `grounds-measure` and `bridges-to-part-iii` targets in prose only; `:252-253` tells the orchestrator to hand agents \"the dataset channel list\" that the plan never supplies.\n→ **Observed, a perfect internal control:** `bridges-to-fcm` resolves **68/68 (100%)**. `grounds-measure` resolves **0/37** across 27 free-text strings, while `corpus/index/Boredom Experiment (VR Attention Study)/` has five stable ids (`bex-00`..`bex-04`) that not one edge names. `bridges-to-part-iii`: 0/128 across 122 distinct strings, 95% singletons.\n\n**D14 — The concordance gate checks coverage, not evidence.**\n`VR-PED:129-130` specifies cells as `{construct, condition, sources:[{id, locus, note}]}` with direction of effect; `VR-PED:218-219` gates only that every row maps and every unit appears somewhere.\n→ **Observed:** the executor invented a mechanical co-occurrence join (documented in the artifact's own header, lines 4-6). 348 cell-unit assertions; **only 32 backed by an authored edge — 316 (90.8%) unbacked**; 71 of 94 cells have zero backing. The shipped JSON is `{row, column, units[], n}` — the mandated `locus` and `note` are absent from **100%** of cells. Boredom's is identical: `BOR-SEC:159-160` specified `sources:[{id, locus, note}]`, 91/91 cells shipped as `{construct, measure, units[], n}` with **0 loci and 0 notes**, and the deviation is not in `planCorrections`.\n\n**D15 — Extraction is mandated to a scratch directory and treated as disposable.**\n`TEMPLATE:137-140`, `BOR-SEC:184-186`, `VR-PED:166-171`. `VR-PED:239` *observes* that the previous session's extraction did not persist and still specifies a scratchpad destination.\n→ **Observed:** `In-Game (Calleja 2011)/` records 588–995 line references (`ig-10-incorporation.json:20`: \"Verified directly from `/tmp/calleja-fulltext.txt` lines 5855-6285\"). That file no longer exists. ~1,000 clause-adjacent pointers — the **finest addressing in the entire corpus** — are unresolvable, along with the entry's own falsification notes. VR Pedagogy's fabricated quotation was undiagnosable from the entry's own materials for the same reason.\n\n**D16 — No page-offset model anywhere.**\nThe word \"offset\" appears **0 times** in `TEMPLATE` and 0 times in `BOR-SEC`. Loci must \"carry page anchors\" (`TEMPLATE:164`) but nothing establishes or verifies the pdf-index → printed-page mapping, and nothing anticipates a non-constant one.\n→ **Observed:** Aristotle — 33 of 34 unit records carry `pdf_pages` from a superseded linear offset, errors up to **47 pages**; `bekker-index` has 101 of 188 loci off by >2 pages. Rickert — `rickert-structured/manifest.json:7` declares `pdf_page_offset: 20`, which is wrong **and** drifts to 15. The correct pattern exists only outside the template: `Uncomfortable .../us-literary-loci-concordance.json` declares `page_offset_rule: \"book p.n = PDF p.n + 10\"`.\n\n**D17 — Registration is a hand-edit to a hardcoded dict at the END of the pipeline.**\n`TEMPLATE:190-197`, gated \"do LAST\" at `:200-201`.\n→ **Observed:** `TEXT_DIRS` holds 19 hardcoded directories against 27 on disk. **8 of 27 entries are unregistered**, including the two richest claim assets in the repo — Dissertation (982 line-anchored claims, 8-tier taxonomy, 841 typed edges) and Veri(dis)similitude (157 stable-id claim rows). RDR2 Secondary states the reason: registering would require hand-authoring a §3A node list, \"a semantic stretch\", so the cluster is \"consumed directly by agents (read as files)\" — which no code implements.\n\n**D18 — The gate list is a checklist in the plan; no artifact is required.**\n`TEMPLATE:216-229`, `BOR-SEC:256-265`, `VR-PED:213-224`, `BEX-ANCHOR:183-186`. `NEWMEDIA` has no gates section at all.\n→ **Observed:** **2 of 27 entries** have a `quality-gates-report.md` (Wendt, RDR2) and **neither was template-built**; 1 has machine-readable metrics. Boredom's only surviving gate evidence is prose strings inside two JSONs (`\"SATISFIED 55/55\"`, `\"gate\": 4`). The template also *abstracted away* artifacts its own precedents produced unbidden: Phantasia's `_synthesis/render-validation.txt` (mmdc version, per-graph counts, PASS table) and RDR2's \"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\" section both stopped appearing once the template replaced hand-written plans.\n\n**D19 — The deliverable is redefined as a node, so the entry is right-sized at 7 records.**\n`BEX-ANCHOR:96`: \"Its value is the node itself + its outbound edges … it is NOT a binding substrate.\"\n→ **Observed:** 9 files, 7 nodes, 0 unit records, 0 runtime edges for a ~92 GB, 8-subject, 3-condition, 7-channel dataset with 24 episodes × 7 instrument items already tabulated. Three plans totalling 795 lines produced 9 files.\n\n**D20 — A PII gate that forbids verification.**\n`BEX-ANCHOR:101-105`: \"Do NOT `ls`/`find` inside `Subjects/` … take structure/counts from `vle-02`/the brief.\"\n→ **Observed:** channel contents were copied from the plan's own §2.2 table instead of checked. `ch-obs | session video | … OBS posture/fidget/watch-glance` (`BEX-ANCHOR:133`) shipped verbatim into the canonical node at commit `48ac09a96`. **It was false — no body camera was ever recorded**, requiring corrective commit `2f4e3ed97` eight days later. Because node definitions are the only text that reaches `compiled-index.json`, a fabricated fact went straight to runtime. `scripts/boredom-o9/README.md` later states the opposite policy: raw-tree inspection *is* authorized.\n\n**D21 — A consent restriction applied as an entry-wide granularity ceiling.**\n`BEX-ANCHOR:106-109`: the entry \"does not commit the full per-subject 24-row matrix.\" That matrix **is** the claim layer — 8 × 3 × 7 = 168 addressable, anonymised, already-collected data claims.\n→ **Observed:** `bex-01-selfreport-record.md` carries 4 aggregate lines and 4 named cases — a ceiling of ~8 assertions for a 24-episode instrument — and violates its own no-duplication rule anyway by reproducing `vle-02`'s aggregate block.\n\n**D22 — A deferral with no re-open trigger became permanent.**\n`BEX-ANCHOR:110-112` declares four channels \"declared-but-unprocessed\"; `BOR-SEC:274-275` authorizes `****** UNVERIFIED:` bridges \"rather than blocking.\"\n→ **Observed:** O-9 processing was executed **the same day** the entry shipped (commit `b766783a5`, 764 lines under `scripts/boredom-o9/`, all 8 subjects, Friedman + Wilcoxon + Holm, **pupil dilation Boring < Clinical in all 8 subjects, p = 0.008**). `scripts/boredom-o9/.gitignore` excludes `out/`. The index still reads \"UNPROCESSED (O-9 deferred)\" at `book-level-ontology.md:49,:70,:77,:84` and `manifest.json:26,:28,:29,:30,:45`. **The only significant statistical finding this dataset has produced is nowhere in `corpus/index/`.** Separately, the Boredom Experiment entry was built 2026-07-16 and Boredom Secondary still carries 37 unresolved `grounds-measure` edges and 12 `****** UNVERIFIED: dataset entry not built` mappings.\n\n**D23 — A phase report used as a creation plan.**\n`NEWMEDIA:135-139` — no gates, no acceptance criteria, no definition of done; one quality clause (\"verify every verbatim via `archon evidence find … --mode exact`\").\n→ **Observed:** three entries, 0 structured records, 0 edges, 0 gate reports. `NEWMEDIA:158` defines the unit as \"drafting loci\" — quotes selected for one dissertation passage — which caps records at what the passage needs: **4 loci for a 47-page MA thesis**, 8 for 4 sources, 8 for 3 sources.\n\n**D24 — The verification payload was captured and thrown away.**\n`NEWMEDIA:135` asks the author to run `evidence find --mode exact` and record the verdict. The tool returns provenance **including a bounding box** — the report itself writes \"provenance: exact-1.00 (sim 1.00) · bbox ✓\".\n→ **Observed:** the string `bbox ✓` appears 45+ times across the three entries. **Zero bounding-box coordinates are stored anywhere in `corpus/index/`.** The audit's finding that nothing in 1,758 files carries a bbox is not a missing resource — it is a **discarded** one, at authoring time, in every one of those 22 loci.\n\n**D25 — Fabricated quotation shipped, undetectable by every defined gate.**\n`VR-PED:31-32` constrains quotation **length** and nothing else; no plan in the repo has a fidelity requirement.\n→ **Observed:** `ped-sec-29-biocca-burgoon-harms-robust-theory.md:7` asserts, inside a sentence tagged `(FE, p.456-457)` and therefore presented as the source's own published claim, the phrase \"sense of being in the place\". The source reads \"being in the **virtual** place\" (extracted lines 40-41) and, separately, \"the sense of the place\" (line 44). The shipped string occurs nowhere in the source. At 6 words it clears the 12-word allowance; there is no fidelity gate; the named detector does not exist.\n\n**D26 — The identity freeze outranked the source.**\n`VR-PED:90` assigns `ped-sec-14`, slug `colin-vr-desktop-2d`, author \"Colin et al.\" from a three-page metadata skim; `VR-PED:105-110` derives folder and filenames from that string; `TEMPLATE:78-79` makes the manifest authoritative but says nothing about storage handles.\n→ **Observed:** \"Colin\" is Robin **Colin Alexander Barrett**'s middle name. The executor caught it at Phase 1 and **declined to fix it**, recording in `planCorrections` that it kept the id/slug/folder \"to match the plan's own section 1C table so cross-references stay stable.\" Today the folder is still `Colin et al. - VR Desktop-3D and 2D (2022)/` while all 30 provenance tags inside read `FAITHFUL-Barrett et al.` — a permanent internal contradiction. Three unresolved citation-year errors and one mis-linkage sit in `_synthesis/citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md`, still unapplied per its line 52.\n\n### 2.2 HIGH — causal chains (compressed)\n\n| # | Plan instruction | Built artifact | Observed defect | Downstream |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| D27 | `TEMPLATE:115,:173` / `BOR-SEC:213` \"concat + dedup\", **no key** | `global-edges.csv` | Boredom keyed `(src,rel,tgt)` → 1,897 rows, silently collapsing **18 locus-distinct rows**; VR Pedagogy keyed `(src,rel,tgt,locus)` → lost 0 but destroyed **2 non-duplicate** edges differing only in `note`; shared helper `normalize-edges.py:268` hardcodes the destructive key | Evidence loss is unrecoverable and unreported; 66 count-mismatch defects corpus-wide |\n| D28 | `TEMPLATE:162` states columns once, for the per-unit file only | four sibling clusters shipped **four different** `global-edges.csv` headers (Boredom `+unit`; VR-Ped bare; RDR2 `unit` first; Phantasia with `edge_id`, `domain`, split evidence columns) | no cross-entry union of edges is possible | corpus-wide: **47 distinct edge-CSV header dialects**, 19,770 rows, ~9,762 distinct triples, read by nothing |\n| D29 | `TEMPLATE:219` `≥12·N` post-dedup edges | never binds (Boredom 1,897 vs floor 660; VR-Ped 1,129 vs 408) | **anti-correlated with evidence**: a more destructive dedup key makes the gate easier to pass | shortfalls undetectable |\n| D30 | `VR-PED:213,:216` hard-codes the derived numeral (`≥276`, \"N = 23\"); `VR-PED:226` says the G0 decisions are CONFIRMED, \"do not re-open\" | N drifted 23 → 34 with an entire unplanned Strand F | correct floor was 408; checkbox still reads 276; `:215` still says \"23 unit trios\" | every downstream numeral stale; nothing re-gated |\n| D31 | `TEMPLATE:167` \"author the synthesis layer YOURSELF in the main loop\"; budget `1+N+N` (`:205-207`) | Phase 3 reconciles 2,588 sub-items + 3,815 edges in one context | locus-blind dedup + 162-value stance vocabulary uncaught | at claim level a 55-source cluster is 5,000–27,500 records — beyond any single context |\n| D32 | `TEMPLATE:208-210` \"self-author any gaps\"; completeness = file existence | 55/55 and 34/34 trios exist | readings per unit range **0 to 30**; three units ship **zero** readings and pass every gate (`bor-sec-21` at 2,581 words, `-29`, `-40`) | no record survives of which units were agent-built vs orchestrator-invented |\n| D33 | `TEMPLATE:168-172` node bullets have no id; compiler merges globally by `name.lower()` (`:1310-1349`) | 68 Boredom nodes, 0 ids; 508 back-references keyed on English strings that already disagree | **20 fused cross-entry rows** with concatenated provenance; no compiled node carries an id field at all | the only address for any node at runtime is its display name |\n| D34 | `TEMPLATE:90-98` \"adapt names to the domain, keep ≤12\" | every cluster coined its own relations | Boredom `treats-construct`/`operationalizes-measure`; VR-Ped its own; Phantasia a `domain` column no sibling has | 645 distinct relation values corpus-wide; edges not comparable |\n| D35 | `TEMPLATE:114,:176-177` mandates `.md` **and** `.json` twins | compiler reads only `.md` (verified) | In-Game and Uncomfortable each authored **18 canonical POSITIONS** into `book-level-ontology.json` — all 36 reach nothing | Uncomfortable carries **two disjoint concept registries** in one directory (`C-US-01..40` vs `US-C-001..036`) |\n| D36 | `BOR-SEC:261` hard-codes obligations to strand letters | Strand G grew 2 → 11 units under user instruction | **7 of 11 Strand-G units carry no bridge edge**; 20% of the entry has no relational floor | gates never regenerated on scope change |\n| D37 | `TEMPLATE:150` captures extraction quality as one self-assessed `ocr_confidence` string | no character-fidelity check; \"encoding\", \"ligature\", \"diacritic\" appear nowhere | `ig-10-deep.json:425-430` documents hand-repairing `difﬁ culty`, `sufﬁ cient`, `ﬁ gurative` (pypdfium2 fi/ff/fl drop); `uex-analysis/book-level-ontology.md:27` ships **`Wohnhulle`** for `Wohnhülle` — and that is the file the compiler reads | `compile-corpus-index.py:157-163` silently falls back to latin-1 on UTF-8 failure, converting a decode error into mojibake; 13 encoding-corruption defects |\n| D38 | `VR-PED:184,:220` requires ≥1 bridge edge **per unit**, where bridges are by definition `anticipatory-application` speculation (`:141-143`) | 117 P-tagged edges = 10.4% of the store; 24 more authored then retired wholesale | the gate mandates a **minimum quantity of our own unfalsifiable interpretation** | `VR-PED:20,:132` explicitly authorised edges to an anchor flagged NOT YET BUILT — dangling references as planned output |\n| D39 | `TEMPLATE:182-185` `≤25` edge cap on the cross-pipeline `.mmd` | VR-Ped's graph states in its own header (lines 4-6) that it was aggregated to strand level \"to stay within the 25-edge Phase-4 cap\" | 117 unit-level bridges reduced to integer labels on 8 arrows | a **rendering** constraint promoted into a data-model constraint |\n| D40 | `BOR-SEC:190` commissions `phase0-overview.md` once, never reconciled | still reads \"Final unit count: 46\" and \"46 → 45 units, pending a user decision\" | manifest says 55, disk holds 55; the 11-chapter Hadjioannou expansion appears nowhere in it | the doc still ends \"Pausing here for go-ahead\" |\n| D41 | `BOR-SEC:258` \"~44 units\" | shipped 55 (+25%) and passed | the tilde makes the gate unfalsifiable at 40 or 60 | it also cannot see the one real gap: `units/` is an **empty directory**; `bor-sec-00-corpus-overview` (required at `:105`, `:138`) was never created |\n| D42 | `BOR-SEC:44-85` inventory assembled without per-file verification | 3 errors | \"Standish 2015\" names a paper that does not exist (real: Mansikka 2008; on-disk PDF is a mislabeled Mertel 2020 duplicate) → build-abort/restore cycle; \"Lindley & Nacke\" reverses the byline; **two Elpidorou 2018 files omitted** — which were the sole in-cluster grounding for the plan's own debate axis and construct row | a hole in the plan's designed anchor, caused by an unverified table |\n| D43 | `BOR-SEC:92` asserts a file \"IS the single extracted paper\" | `pdfinfo` shows **727 pages**, md5-identical to the full proceedings | executor had to invent an `awk RS='\\f'` page-boundary search | a full investigative detour on an unverified premise |\n| D44 | `EVAL`/`MIGRATION` assume an injectable index path | none exists | `jsonl-loaders.ts:198-200` hard-resolves `<cwd>/corpus/index/compiled-index.json`; `corpus-index-provider.ts:73-77` **explicitly ignores** its `indexPath` argument | **no A/B of any index is runnable in the live tree**; the sandbox worked only via an unmerged fork honouring `CORPUS_INDEX_PATH` |\n| D45 | `MIGRATION:94` \"Both authors MUST be cited with direct textual evidence\" | 42 of 72 hooks have an empty `targetConcept`; `cross-author-utils.ts:473-474` makes `t.includes('')` always true | 4 of 6 simulated topics select an empty-target hook and render `<-> ? ()` under a MUST-cite directive labelled \"verified, high-confidence\" | **an anti-gate**: it compels fabrication. 525 of 552 sandbox bridge candidates (95%) were generated against empty anchors; 85% came back \"unrelated\" |\n| D46 | `MIGRATION:138` hard gate = line-for-line parity with the live TS retriever | requires reproducing caps 12/3/5 + 1 bridge | that ceiling is exactly what made a 4.3× claim scale-up **regress** quality by 0.005 and drop six named authors from the prose | parity with the concept-level contract is the wrong bar |\n| D47 | `USAGE:377-380` \"Adding New Texts\", 4 steps | omits registration in `TEXT_DIRS` entirely | 8 of 27 entries followed it and reach runtime with zero records | the N=1 path in the only usage-facing plan is broken |\n| D48 | `VLE` manifest's own governing instruction: \"gates deferred to post-run review\" | the review never happened | 7 of 18 nodes carry counts their own units superseded on 2026-07-23/24; the ontology file is the only file that compiles | **100% of what VLE serves to runtime is stale**, including the `E-SHA 67` figure live in `compiled-index.json:155` and the 4.3-vs-1.2 figure copied into **12 live files** of a sibling entry |\n\n### 2.3 Code facts I re-verified independently\n\n| Claim | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| No verbatim-quote detector exists in `scripts/` | **CONFIRMED** — 30 scripts; only `substitute-quote-ids.py` is quote-adjacent |\n| No `*.schema.json` exists in the repo proper | **CONFIRMED** — only vendored `node_modules` / `.venv` hits |\n| `mmdc` IS installed | **CONFIRMED** — `/home/dalton/.nvm/versions/node/v22.22.0/bin/mmdc` → `@mermaid-js/mermaid-cli` |\n| The compiler reads `book-level-ontology.md` → falls back to `cluster-ontology.md`, and warns only when **missing** | **CONFIRMED** at `compile-corpus-index.py:1217-1229` |\n| `collect_tension_edges` opens only `<analysis_subdir>/tension-edges.json` | **CONFIRMED** at `:1253-1274` |\n| `collect_cross_pipeline_hooks` globs **only** the Aristotle directory | **CONFIRMED** at `:1234-1250` — a fact no plan mentions |\n\n### 2.4 REFUTED / adjudicated (inter-reviewer contradictions)\n\n| Contested claim | Source | Verdict | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| \"A repo verbatim detector exists and Boredom passes it\" | gold-standard reviewer, on `BOR-SEC:262` | **REFUTED** | No such script (re-verified). The \"pass\" is an unaided grep for long curly-quoted spans, not the plan's named tool. |\n| \"mmdc is not installed in this environment\" | `RDR2 Secondary/_synthesis/quality-gates-report.md` | **REFUTED** | `mmdc` v11.14.0 is installed. The entry's own gate deferral rests on a false premise — an entry-level self-attestation error, and a reason to never accept narration as gate evidence. |\n| \"The concordance gate degenerates at N=1\" | template + boredom reviewers | **REFUTED as stated** | Phantasia's concordance is keyed `loci_by_work` — **source × locus**, not unit × unit. At N=1 it becomes exactly the one row of locus cells that one article fills, which *is* the addressable payload. The defect is the ≤15×15 cap and the presence-matrix rendering, not the idea. |\n| \"Contested readings are inherently cross-source and collapse at N=1\" | template + boredom reviewers | **PARTIALLY REFUTED** | VR Pedagogy's `CR-01` and `CR-03` contest **Short et al. (1976)** and the **SSQ** — neither a cluster unit. Re-based on named *external* interlocutors the record survives intact at N=1. What is genuinely unmeasurable is its *format*: `contested-readings.md` is free prose with `**CR-NN.**` run-in markers, 18 declared vs 21 regex hits. |\n| \"The `≥12·N` edge floor collapses at N=1\" | template reviewer | **PARTIALLY REFUTED** | The per-unit floors at `TEMPLATE:162` (12/20/35) already bind at N=1 by construction. The cluster restatement is **redundant**, not collapsing. The real defect is that it counts post-dedup rows (D29). |\n| \"Concepts require multiple sources\" | implicit in strand design `TEMPLATE:68-70` | **REFUTED** | 9 of 41 gold-cluster (Phantasia) concepts are already **single-unit**. Concept extraction is an entry-scope operation. |\n\n**Net effect of the adjudication:** only **three** gates in the whole family genuinely evaluate to nothing at N=1 — documented debates, the intra-cluster citation network, and the scholarly-evolution arc. The \"everything collapses at N=1\" framing is overstated and would, if carried into the new plan, wrongly delete recoverable structure.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The gate system, judged\n\n### 3.1 Gate-by-gate table\n\n**Legend:** *Code?* = enforced by a program that can fail. *Right?* = measures the property it claims to.\n\n| # | Gate (plan:line) | Threshold | Code? | Measurable? | Right? | At N=1 | At claim level | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| G-1 | N units × 3 files on disk (`TEMPLATE:218`) | presence | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | trivially true | useless — 3 files can hold 5 or 500 records | **The only gate that binds** (100% pass on 55/55, 34/34, 12/12) and the weakest. Blind to `units/` being empty (`BOR-SEC:105`). Nested chapter units break the obvious glob (45 of 56 found). |\n| G-2 | ≥12·N dedup global edges (`TEMPLATE:219`) | 12N | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | redundant with per-unit floors, not vacuous | off by 1–2 orders | **Never binds** (2.8–2.9× over) and **anti-correlated** with evidence preservation |\n| G-3 | 8–12 documented debates (`TEMPLATE:219`) | band | ✗ | ✗ (no format) | ✓ in kind | **zero by construction** — all 12 Phantasia + 11 Boredom axes are multi-unit, min 3 | a fixed band *caps* recorded disagreement | **Manufactures content.** VR-Ped `DA-07`/`DA-08` cite exactly one unit each; Boredom flags 3 of 11 as `constructedByCluster` |\n| G-4 | 8–12 contested readings (`TEMPLATE:219`) | band | ✗ | ✗ | ✓ | **survives** if re-based on external interlocutors | should be per-claim `contested_by[]` | Unmeasurable for want of a format; VR-Ped shipped 18 against the band, unflagged |\n| G-5 | ≥50 terminology lemmas (`TEMPLATE:220`) | 50 | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | arbitrary but computable | orthogonal to claims | 20× spread in lemmas/unit across passing entries (Phantasia 213/8, Boredom 72/55). Artifact unreachable. |\n| G-6 | ≥max(10, N/4) intra-cluster citations (`TEMPLATE:220`) | 10 | ✗ | ✗ (incompatible artifacts) | ✓ | **unsatisfiable** — a source cannot cite itself 10× | meaningless within one source | Taught executors to talk past gates: RDR2 reframed 4-vs-15 as \"a finding, not a shortfall\" |\n| G-7 | Concordance complete (`TEMPLATE:221-222`) | coverage | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | **survives** if keyed source×locus | invites a co-occurrence join → 90.8% unbacked | **Self-defeating escape hatch**: \"(or `****** UNVERIFIED:`)\" means absence passes. Boredom logged `SATISFIED 12/12` where all twelve are placeholders |\n| G-8 | ≥1 bridge edge per anchor-strand unit (`TEMPLATE:223-224`) | ≥1 | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | **applies** — best-formed gate in §8 | needs lifting to per-claim | Checks presence, never **resolution**. `grounds-measure` = 0/37 resolved and the gate passed |\n| G-9 | No ≥25-word verbatim (`TEMPLATE:225`) | 25 w | ✗ | ✗ (no tool) | ✗ | unchanged | **actively hostile** — the clause is the payload | Threshold internally inconsistent (25 vs 30). Applied to public-domain sources. Drove truncation to exactly 24 words |\n| G-10 | Provenance tags \"throughout\" (`TEMPLATE:225`) | — | ✗ | ✗ (no unit of text) | ✓ in kind | unchanged | needs to be a required field | Only **67 of 463** Boredom readings carry a tag value; 201 null. A writing convention, not a field |\n| G-11 | 5 Mermaid graphs render; ≤25 edges (`TEMPLATE:226`) | 5 / 25 | ✗ | ✗ (no command named) | ✗ | 2 of 5 render empty | render cap ≠ data cap | `mmdc` IS installed. 2 of 15 `.mmd`-bearing entries have any render record; 67 `.mmd` files encode 1,544 arrow-edges with no adapter |\n| G-12 | Parseable `## 3A` (`TEMPLATE:227`) | presence | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ | unchanged | node count invariant to claim count | **Measures a token the parser ignores.** Passes with 0 nodes; passes while 204/701 nodes are corrupted |\n| G-13 | Compiler runs clean (`TEMPLATE:227`) | — | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | always passes | always passes | **Unfalsifiable.** `main()` always returns 0; 0 warnings while 55 tension records were discarded |\n| G-14 | Compiled counts verified by reading (`TEMPLATE:227-228`) | — | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | works | needs extension to claims/spans/loci | **Best gate in §8** — and human-executed, scoped to node totals only, with no declared expectation to compare against. Certified 2.3% reachability as success |\n| G-15 | Verbatim detector clean (`TEMPLATE:228`) | — | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | n/a | would forbid the target record | **Names a tool that does not exist** |\n| G-16 | Backups + G0 + G1, no commit before G1 (`TEMPLATE:229`) | — | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | applies | applies | **Sound — preserve.** Only weakness: G1 sits last, which is why 8 entries were never registered. Boredom's `.backups/` does **not** contain the two files `BOR-SEC:243` names |\n| G-17 | PII grep empty (`BEX-ANCHOR:184-185`) | 0 hits | ✗ | ✓ | ✗ (hygiene, not index quality) | works | scales | **Keep — the only genuinely machine-checkable gate in 795 lines.** But sever it from the inspection ban that caused D20 |\n| G-18 | 24-cell file coverage with explicit flags (`BEX-v1:259-260`) | 24/24 | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | excellent — computable denominator | generalises perfectly | **The model for every coverage gate the new plan needs.** Never evaluated: the entry it gated was cancelled |\n| G-19 | Deletion-diff invariants (`BEX-ANCHOR:85-89`) | 24 rows / non-orphaning / before→after delta | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | fully defined | generalises | **Best gate in the series.** Port wholesale as the template for corrective passes |\n| G-20 | Phase-V drafting validation, 7 items (`USAGE:200-210`) | mixed | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ | vacuous — gates a *run*, not an entry | blind | Produced zero artifacts across 27 entries |\n| G-21 | `--citation-min-pass-rate 0.85` / `--citation-max-hallucinations 0` (`USAGE:161-162`) | 0.85 / 0 | **✓** | ✓ | ✗ | n/a to entry creation | passes while unlocatable | Real and enforced — but the recorded run shows passRate exactly 0.85, 3 hallucinations \"corrected\", and **`missingPageNumbers` 17 of 20** |\n| G-22 | H3 \"B traceability ≈100% at char level\" (`EVAL:186-188`) | ~100% | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | checkable on one source | **the right predicate** | **The one gate in all four eval/migration plans that measures the right thing.** Actual: 4,615/4,961 = 93.0% with spans, 226 `quote_match` false, `match_ratio` min 0.083. Never run |\n| G-23 | Process firewall — draft fully in one condition before opening the other (`EVAL:89-95`) | — | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | designed for N=1 | matters more | **Best methodological gate in the corpus.** Auditable via tool-call logs |\n| G-24 | Double locus `(p.NN / pdf NN)` on every citation (`WENDT:129`) | 100% | ✗ | ✓ | ✓ | applies | extends to a triple locus | **307/307 = 100% compliance.** Precisely specified + regex-checkable + per-record. The only gate in the family with perfect compliance |\n\n### 3.2 The cross-unit-gate argument — does it hold?\n\n**Partially. It is overstated by roughly half.**\n\n*Holds.* Three gates genuinely evaluate to nothing at N=1, verified against the gold cluster: **documented debates** (12/12 Phantasia and 11/11 Boredom axes are multi-unit, minimum 3 units each), the **intra-cluster citation network** (zero siblings ⇒ structurally zero, and the floor of 10 makes it not merely vacuous but **permanently failing**), and the **scholarly-evolution arc** (a date range that is a point). These three, and only these, belong in an optional GROUP layer with `N/A-by-construction` semantics.\n\n*Does not hold.* Four claimed collapses are false (§2.4): the **concordance** keyed source×locus is the N=1 payload; **contested readings** survive when re-based on external interlocutors; the **12·N edge floor** is redundant rather than collapsing because per-unit floors already bind; and **concepts** are already single-unit in 9 of 41 gold cases.\n\n*The real defect the argument obscures.* The gates that fail at N=1 fail at N=55 too, for a different reason: they are **aggregate counts with no per-source denominator**. Boredom passed every numeric gate while three of its units shipped zero claims. Fixing N=1 by adding skip semantics is necessary but not sufficient; the substantive fix is to make every gate an **intensive per-source quantity** (records per 1,000 source words, locator-resolution rate, schema-validity rate, span-fidelity rate), which is simultaneously meaningful at N=1 and binding at N=55.\n\n### 3.3 Gates satisfied by agent self-attestation rather than by a check\n\n**Every gate in the family except two.** Nothing in `TEMPLATE`, `BOR-SEC`, `VR-PED`, `BEX-*` or `NEWMEDIA` runs a program that can fail. The two exceptions are `USAGE:161-162` (real CLI flags on a *drafting* run, not entry creation) and, arguably, `BEX-ANCHOR:184` (a grep, still executed by narration).\n\nNamed, self-attested gates:\n\n1. G-1 file presence — asserted by the orchestrator that self-authored the gaps (`TEMPLATE:208-210`)\n2. G-2 edge floor — counted by eye\n3. G-3 debates — Boredom's own `debate-map.json` embeds `constructedByCluster: 3`\n4. G-4 contested readings — 18 shipped against a stated 8–12; nobody counted\n5. G-5 lemmas — self-counted\n6. G-6 intra-cluster citations — `citation-network.json` embeds its own verdict `{required:10, deliveredTotal:65, satisfied:true}`; VR-Ped's has no `links` array so the same gate is not even computable on both\n7. G-7 concordance — `rowToFcmGate: \"SATISFIED 11/11\"`, `columnToChannelGate: \"SATISFIED 12/12\"` as prose strings **inside the artifact being judged**\n8. G-9 verbatim — RDR2: \"per-unit agents verified (longest ~19 w)\"\n9. G-10 provenance \"throughout\" — no unit of measure\n10. G-11 mermaid render — RDR2 deferred it on a false premise\n11. G-12 §3A parseable — passes for files with zero parseable nodes\n12. G-13 compiler clean — cannot fail\n13. G-14 compiled counts — a human comparing numbers with no declared expectation\n14. G-15 verbatim detector — the tool does not exist\n15. G-18/G-19 — well designed, never executed\n16. `BOR-SEC:243` backups — the two named files are absent from `.backups/`\n\n**Structural root:** the producer and the judge are the same agent, and every gate verdict that exists is embedded in the artifact it judges. That is the single most important thing the new plan must break.\n\n---\n\n## 4. What the plans never say\n\nRanked by damage done. Each row: the gap, the plan location where it should have been, and the measured consequence.\n\n| Rank | Unspecified | Where it belonged | Damage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **What a CLAIM is** — no record type, no id, no granularity rule, no yield target | `TEMPLATE:159-161`, `BOR-SEC:165,:204` | The entire granularity ceiling. ~7 records/source vs 50–500 target. Only `DISS-PIPE` ever wrote a definition down (\"a discrete proposition that could plausibly be true or false, contested or supported\", with a worked 3-claims-in-one-sentence example) — and it is the only entry that hit the target |\n| 2 | **What a CLAUSE is** — no sentence index, char span or bbox is named or requested anywhere | everywhere | Zero clause addresses in 1,758 files. The finest locators in the corpus arrived **incidentally**: Bekker line pairs (2,323), In-Game line ranges (995, now dead), RDR2 timestamps (529) and frame ids (1,040), VLE respondent×item keys |\n| 3 | **Element schemas for the seven unit-JSON arrays** | `TEMPLATE:159-161`, `BOR-SEC:204` | 42 incompatible shapes over 2,924 sub-items in one entry; 9 sub-schemas; no consumer can join them |\n| 4 | **`tension-edges.json` and its `node_a`/`node_b` contract** | `TEMPLATE:112-124`, `BOR-SEC:119-132` | 4 of 11 files yield zero; 55–119 records discarded silently; template-built clusters have none at all |\n| 5 | **Which artifacts the loader reads** | `TEMPLATE:187-197`, `BEX-v1:50-54`, `USAGE:377-380` | 97.7% of Boredom, 99% of VR Pedagogy, 8 of 9 Boredom-Experiment files unreachable. `book-level-ontology.json` twins: 36 canonical positions lost |\n| 6 | **Controlled values for stance / tier / type / role / disposition** | `BOR-SEC:165-167` | 162 stance values with 195 nulls; 15 uncontrolled `claim_type` values in the sandbox; ~36 type values corpus-wide |\n| 7 | **An id grammar below the unit + uniqueness scope** | `BOR-SEC:101-106`, `TEMPLATE:73` | 37 colliding `C1..C22`; 296 unaddressable readings; Wendt 91 id-less / 20 colliding; two disjoint registries in Uncomfortable; 10 id-prefix + 10 id-collision defects |\n| 8 | **The dedup key** for `global-edges.csv` | `TEMPLATE:115,:173`, `BOR-SEC:213` | 18 locus-distinct rows destroyed in one entry, 2 note-distinct edges in another, from the *same sentence* |\n| 9 | **The page-offset model** (the word \"offset\" appears 0×) | `TEMPLATE:54`, Phase 0 | Aristotle 33/34 records wrong by up to 47 pages; 101/188 Bekker loci off by >2; Rickert's offset wrong **and** drifting |\n| 10 | **Retention/hashing of the extracted text** | `TEMPLATE:137-140` | ~1,000 In-Game clause pointers dead; VR-Ped's entire evidential basis irreproducible; the fabricated quotation undiagnosable from the entry |\n| 11 | **Storage of retrieval provenance** (`bbox`, `char_span`) | `NEWMEDIA:135` | 45+ `bbox ✓` ticks, zero coordinates — a discarded clause-level address system |\n| 12 | **The parser's alias/parenthetical transformation** | `TEMPLATE:168-172` | 204/701 nodes poisoned; `technological`, `control`, `gaze-based`, `anyone`, `publicness` in the corpus-wide greedy-match list |\n| 13 | **Record density targets per source** | `TEMPLATE:154-155` gives *word* budgets instead | 8.4 readings/unit; 3 units at zero; inverse density-to-length relation (Holmqvist 53pp → 0.19 readings/page vs Aho 3pp → 1.67) |\n| 14 | **Gate-result artifacts** | `TEMPLATE:216-229` §8 | 2 of 27 entries have a gates report; 1 has metrics |\n| 15 | **Whether negative claims are records** | `TEMPLATE:158` asks for a \"Not treated:\" prose line | `bor-sec-30` names 8 explicitly-absent measures and `bor-sec-13` 3 absent constructs — in prose, in **no** JSON array. A machine-checkable weakness class, written and discarded |\n| 16 | **Encoding / ligature / diacritic policy** (all three words appear 0×) | `TEMPLATE:137-150` | Uexküll ships four German orthographies and the **corrupted** one reaches runtime; 13 encoding defects |\n| 17 | **A global relation & type registry** | `TEMPLATE:90-98` | 645 relation values, 47 CSV dialects, 8 tension shapes; cross-entry union impossible |\n| 18 | **Rights tiering** | `TEMPLATE:44` hardcodes \"all sources are copyrighted\" | Suppression applied to the user's own work and to public-domain texts; two entries carry explicit suppression audits |\n| 19 | **The N=1 path** | whole of Phase −1 | No single-source entry was ever built from the template; thin entries silently dropped the machinery instead of adapting it |\n| 20 | **A derivation/fidelity marker** distinguishing agent-read from self-authored | `TEMPLATE:208-210` authorises self-authoring | No build provenance anywhere; a fabricated unit is indistinguishable from a read one |\n| 21 | **What happens when a deferral clears** | `BOR-SEC:274-275`, `BEX-ANCHOR:110-112` | 37 + 12 + 3 unresolved markers 13 days after the blocker cleared; a p=0.008 finding never entered the index |\n| 22 | **Manifest re-derivation from disk** | `TEMPLATE:78-79` declares it authoritative at Phase 0 | 66 count-mismatch defects — the largest single class |\n| 23 | **Idempotency / re-run / growth contract** | absent entirely | Incremental growth of an index is undefined; Dissertation carries two identical full run-histories with no rule for which counts |\n| 24 | **A query surface** | `USAGE`, `EVAL` | Zero references to `claims.jsonl` / `concept-mentions.jsonl` anywhere in `src/` or `scripts/`. `EVAL:126` asks an agent to consult 14,811 JSONL rows with no tool |\n| 25 | **Index-path injectability** | no plan | Blocks every possible A/B measurement (~20 LOC) |\n| 26 | **Nested/chapter unit policy** | `TEMPLATE:127` | Boredom's 11 nested units invisible to the obvious enumeration |\n| 27 | **Whether `-00-` meta-records count toward N** | `TEMPLATE:73` | Every N-scaled gate ambiguous by one |\n| 28 | **Source admissibility preconditions** | absent | `ptf-01` (identical per-page `text_hash`, all verbatims UNVERIFIED) and `riv-02` (unverified venue) were authored into canonical nodes |\n| 29 | **A downstream-citation index** | absent | A corrected VLE figure left 12 stale live copies in a sibling entry |\n| 30 | **Plan supersession / fact migration** | absent | `BEX-v2`'s byte-verified 12-column schema, 24-cell table, ~2.99 Hz cadence and S05 corroboration stranded in a plan file; the built entry states \"@ 120 Hz\" with no caveat |\n| 31 | **Cost and budget model** | absent | Programme scoped by guesswork despite $20/3,776-claim and $0.30/run reference points existing |\n| 32 | **`schema_version` stamping** | absent | Only Dissertation stamps one; nothing else can be safely migrated because nothing declares its shape |\n\n---\n\n## 5. What must be preserved\n\nThese are not concessions. Several are the only reason this audit was possible.\n\n**5.1 The two-gate rhythm — G0 before authoring, G1 before commit (`TEMPLATE:100-103`, `:200-201`, `:229`).** G0 fixed Boredom's scope, axes and anchors before 55 agents ran; correcting axes at spec time costs a conversation, correcting them after costs a rebuild. G1 plus \"never commit before sign-off\" plus mandatory timestamped `.backups/` (`TEMPLATE:189`) is the only structural protection in the process. **Keep verbatim; change only *what* G1 is shown** — a machine-readable gates report, not a diff and a sample.\n\n**5.2 `manifest.planCorrections` (`TEMPLATE:214`, `BOR-SEC` execution).** The single best piece of process behaviour in the corpus. Boredom recorded 7 deviations with issue / files / **evidence commands and outputs** / resolution / residual. Correction #7 caught the plan **contradicting itself** (`BOR-SEC:208` Strand A vs `:261` Strand A/B), resolved toward the more specific rule, **refused to fabricate** three `bridges-to-fcm` edges for `bor-sec-15/17/19`, cited per-source evidence for each refusal, and explicitly declined to edit the plan so the contradiction would stay visible. Make it a required artifact with a fixed schema.\n\n**5.3 The no-fabrication norm with an escalation path.** The `bor-sec-18` agent refused to build a unit under a false attribution when its PDF proved to be a mislabeled duplicate, and escalated. Preserve \"refuse and escalate\" as an explicitly sanctioned agent outcome, alongside `****** UNVERIFIED:`.\n\n**5.4 The three-value provenance discipline (`TEMPLATE:38-42`).** `FE` / `FAITHFUL-<AUTHOR>` / `P·anticipatory-application`, with every bridge claim tagged anticipatory and never presented as the source's own. Corpus-wide usage: 2,761 FE, 1,323 P, 1,196 burke-direct, 85 FAITHFUL keys. It is the most consistently applied idea in the whole index and it is exactly what keeps the user's readings separable from the sources'. **Promote from prose convention to a required, closed, validated field.**\n\n**5.5 The 8-tier support taxonomy (`DISS-PIPE:333-341`).** T1-textually-confirmed → T7-overreach → T8-secondary-needed, each with a remediation action. Exercised at scale on 982 records (T3 477, T1 277, T2 78, T5 71, T4 41, T7 22, T6 12, T8 4). This is the field that delivers \"every weakness\" as a **queryable property** rather than a narrative aside. Adopt verbatim.\n\n**5.6 The interpretive-flag pair (`DISS-PIPE` schema).** `interpretive_flag_present` (boolean) **plus** `interpretive_flag_text` carrying the actual hedge from the prose (\"'which I designate as occupying A₃'\"). Quoting the hedge is what makes a tier assignment auditable rather than asserted.\n\n**5.7 The claim record schema and its literal JSONC example (`DISS-PIPE:490-535`).** The only place any plan in this repo writes out a record schema — and the only place a working claim layer resulted. That correlation is not an accident.\n\n**5.8 The granularity rule with a worked decomposition + the anti-inflation cap (`DISS-PIPE`).** \"One proposition = one claim, not one sentence = one claim\", plus a per-section hard cap of 350. Both halves are needed.\n\n**5.9 Anchor discipline — bridge, never re-digest (`TEMPLATE:30-36`).** Pointers to an anchor's unit ids rather than re-explaining its argument. Where the plan enumerated the target ids (`BOR-SEC:24`), resolution was **68/68**. This is what stops ~265 single-source entries becoming ~265 re-explanations of the same books.\n\n**5.10 The de-duplication and haystack rubric (`TEMPLATE:57-67`).** md5-identical DROP; preprint/published MERGE with a `dup-variant` note; >300pp proceedings HAYSTACK with grep-locate and `-f/-l` re-extraction. Concrete, mechanical, and it worked: 49 files → 44 units, with two real salvages from a 727-page volume. Its dispositions persisted into `manifest.excluded` with md5 evidence.\n\n**5.11 Pre-extraction to text, agents given the `.txt` path and never the PDF (`TEMPLATE:137-140`).** Correct for cost and for the known multi-page-image API-400 failure. Only the *destination* is wrong.\n\n**5.12 The OCR-LOW check (`TEMPLATE:141`, `VR-PED:167-170`).** It correctly caught Lombard & Ditton at 0 words; `manifest.ocrAudit` records the range (4,281–21,903 words) and the reasoning for the lowest non-zero count.\n\n**5.13 Hard per-unit numeric floors (`TEMPLATE:162-165`).** 0 violations across 55 units and 34 units. **The mechanism is perfect; only the quantity is wrong.** Keep per-unit hard floors and point them at claims and coverage.\n\n**5.14 The \"Not treated:\" requirement (`TEMPLATE:158`).** Negative evidence, rare in the corpus, and directly serving \"every weakness.\" Promote from a prose line to a typed absence record.\n\n**5.15 The fixed section skeleton (`TEMPLATE:156-158`, `BOR-SEC:200-202`).** It made 55 independently-built analyses structurally comparable — which is the only reason their ~6,300 propositions are minable at all. Keep the outline; **author it as a rendering of records**.\n\n**5.16 The reliability lesson and post-batch sweep (`TEMPLATE:208-210`).** The ~1/8 subagent no-op is real and documented. Keep the sweep; upgrade what it checks from existence to conformance, and delete \"self-author any gaps.\"\n\n**5.17 Exemplar-driven authoring (`TEMPLATE:213`, `BOR-SEC:178`).** Pointing each agent at a named quality bar works. The exemplar must itself be schema-valid and reachable.\n\n**5.18 The double-locus rule (`WENDT:129`).** `(p.NN / pdf NN)` on every citation — **307/307 = 100% compliance**, the only perfect gate in the family. Precisely specified format + regex-checkable + per-record is the recipe. Extend to a triple locus.\n\n**5.19 `BEX-ANCHOR:38-89` — the corrective-pass template.** Regenerate the live list rather than trusting the cache; precision guard for the double-edge unit; non-destruction check that no unit is orphaned; edit the per-unit source of truth then regenerate the aggregate; fix the tally including a confirmed miscount; verify the delta by **reading** the compiled output. It verifiably worked and is the best-specified operation in all the plans. Port wholesale.\n\n**5.20 `BEX-v2:97-148` — data-fact locking.** Every cell of a 24-cell inventory enumerated with explicit exception flags (`ALT-FORMAT`, `CROP2`, `UNCROPPED`, `TYPO`), a closing accounting line (\"21 clean + 3 exceptions … No silent gaps\"), and a schema whose verification locus is named **to the line**. Make it a required artifact, not plan prose.\n\n**5.21 `BEX-v2:311-313` — the runtime-derived anonymisation constraint.** S-codes derived in memory from sorted directory order, never persisted, not even as a hardcoded table in the script. `scripts/boredom-o9/common.py` implements it and processed all 8 subjects with zero leakage — **proof that full processing and PII discipline are compatible**, and that `BEX-ANCHOR:101-105`'s escalation to \"do not even list the directory\" was unnecessary and harmful.\n\n**5.22 `BEX-v2:7` — the worked proof-of-pipeline.** Prove extraction end-to-end on one unit with independent cross-channel corroboration before scaling.\n\n**5.23 The `EVAL:89-95` process firewall.** Draft fully in one condition before opening the other index. Enforceable by tool-call auditing.\n\n**5.24 `EVAL:198-200` (H6).** \"Prose hierarchy on top, atomic provenance underneath, with programmatic verifiability of every assertion.\" That is the target architecture, written down and never built.\n\n**5.25 Analyst self-critique inside artifacts.** Boredom's `emptyColumnNote` diagnosing a category error inherited from the plan's own measure axis and recommending its removal; its `centralFinding` two-route verification; `citation-network.json`'s `methodologicalCaveat`; RDR2's \"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\"; `debate-map.json`'s `constructedByCluster: 3`. **This candour is why the audit was possible.** Make it a named required field rather than a happy accident.\n\n**5.26 `USAGE:275-282` — the anti-hallucination flag stack** (`--whitelist`, `--citation-max-hallucinations 0`, `--citation-enforcement-mode strict`) as the fixed configuration for every harness arm.\n\n**5.27 Corpus-FIRST retrieval policy (`MIGRATION:89`, `COMPARE:28`).** The authored ontology always runs and seeds query expansion; vectors are additive, never a substitute. Keep the policy; change only the granularity of what it returns.\n\n**5.28 Import from per-entry SOURCE files, never from `compiled-index.json` (`MIGRATION:14-17`).** The lossiness is documented and re-verified.\n\n**5.29 The frozen prompt-suite pattern** (`ARTIFACT-MANIFEST.json`: \"FROZEN — must not be modified without incrementing version and recording new SHA\") and the immutable `_run-history/<ts>/` + `_living/latest.md` pattern in `corpus/index/Dissertation/`.\n\n**5.30 `TEMPLATE:8` — the executor discipline itself:** \"every judgment call this plan cannot pre-make is turned into a derivation procedure with a rubric.\" The instinct is exactly right. It simply was never applied to the record schemas — which is where every defect landed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The claim and clause schema — proposed\n\n### 6.1 Design principles\n\n1. **The CLAIM is the atom.** A source is a container of claims. Prose is a *rendering* of records, never an input constraint.\n2. **The CLAUSE is a separate, independently-identified record.** One clause may ground many claims; one claim may span several clauses. Nesting the span inside the claim (as every current entry does) makes reuse impossible.\n3. **Address and text are separable.** The address is always stored; the text's *storage* is universal and its *display* is rights-tiered. This is what dissolves the copyright/granularity conflict at `TEMPLATE:44-45`.\n4. **Ids are the only join key.** Display strings never join.\n5. **Every enum is closed, inline in the plan, and validated.** Free text lives in a sibling `*_note` field.\n\n### 6.2 The CLAUSE record\n\n| Field | Type | Justified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `clause_id` | `<DOC>-CL<nnnnn>`, global | Wendt's 20 collisions and Boredom's 37 prove per-file counters fail |\n| `doc_id` | stable source identity: `sha256(source_file)` + `edition_key` — **never a path** | In-Game addressed `/tmp`; Aristotle addressed \"the PDF\" and a superseded offset poisoned 33/34 records |\n| `text_layer_id` | id of the retained extraction: `{tool, tool_version, exact_command, flags, text_sha256}` | Two extractions of one PDF give different offsets. In-Game's 995 anchors died for want of this one field |\n| `char_start`, `char_end` | int offsets into that text layer | **NET-NEW.** Nothing in 1,758 files carries one. This is the single structural addition that makes the corpus clause-level |\n| `sentence_index` | int | NET-NEW; the graceful degradation target when char offsets are unstable |\n| `line_start`, `line_end` | int | Already in use and cheaply recoverable: In-Game 858–995 refs; Dissertation anchors 982/982 by line |\n| `page_pdf`, `page_printed` | int | Both, always — `WENDT:129`'s 307/307 double-locus rule generalised |\n| `citation_address` | typed union (§6.5) | Aristotle's `bekker-index.json` record shape `{bekker, description, concepts[], pdf_page, unit_id, work}` proves an edition-independent address must coexist with a rendering-specific one |\n| `quote` | verbatim clause text | The 235 Dissertation cached verbatims are the only place a claim and its grounding words are both present and linked |\n| `quote_sha256`, `quote_word_count` | | The hash is the address that survives re-extraction; the count drives the display policy |\n| `normalized_quote` | NFC, ligature-repaired, whitespace-collapsed | `Wohnhulle`/`Wohnhülle`; `difﬁ culty`; four German orthographies in one entry |\n| `rights_tier` | enum: `own-work \\| public-domain \\| licensed \\| third-party-copyright` | The uniform assumption at `TEMPLATE:44` suppressed clauses in Equiano 1789, Radcliffe 1794, Austen 1811, Darwin 1872 and all of Aristotle |\n| `redact_on_render` | bool | Separates storage from display; retires the \"24-word … under ceiling\" truncation practice |\n| `bbox` | `[x0,y0,x1,y1]` \\| null | `archon evidence find --mode exact` already returns it; 45+ `bbox ✓` ticks discarded it |\n| `extraction_probe` | `{ligature_ok, diacritic_ok, words_per_page}` | 13 encoding defects; the corrupted Uexküll orthography is the one that reaches runtime |\n\n### 6.3 The CLAIM record\n\n| Field | Type / enum | Justified by (the entry that proves it earns its place) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `claim_id` | `<ENTRY>-<UNIT>-C<nnnn>`, global, registered | Dissertation declares `claim_id_format: \"DISS-00-C<nnn>\"` → 982 records, zero collisions. Being and Time 108/108 distinct (`BT-D1-U3-P1`); BCAP 146 distinct; VDS 157 distinct. **Counter-proof:** Wendt 91 id-less / 20 colliding |\n| `entry_id`, `unit_id` | required | `compiled-index.json` nodes already carry `units[]`; without them Wendt's per-file `C1` is meaningless |\n| `claim_text` | ≤60 words, our paraphrase | Populated in every claim-bearing entry; canonical name chosen from 6 competing spellings (`claim_text` 422, `tx` 560, `text` 139+142, `claim` 107+108+18+233+55, `statement` 157) |\n| `clause_refs[]` | array of `clause_id` | Uncomfortable's 176 loci records already sit at or below clause level and are referenced by multiple positions |\n| `claim_kind` | **enum:** `assertion \\| definition \\| textual-report \\| interpretation \\| premise \\| conclusion \\| methodological \\| programmatic \\| quotation \\| contrast \\| open-question \\| negative` | Dissertation's `claim_type` is populated 982/982 (the facet is wanted) with **378 distinct values** (it must be closed). `negative` is new, forced by the discarded \"Not treated:\" content |\n| `scope` | **enum:** `book-thesis \\| chapter-thesis \\| section-thesis \\| unit-thesis \\| local-support \\| transitional` | Being and Time's `status` column — the only place argumentative altitude is recorded, and 94% controlled (101/108) |\n| `stance` | **enum (§6.4)** | 162 free values / 195 nulls / 108 hapax in Boredom |\n| `support_tier` | **enum, 8 values, adopted verbatim** (§6.4) | `DISS-PIPE:333-341`, exercised on 982 records. **This field is \"every weakness.\"** |\n| `evidence_type` | **enum (§6.4)** | Von Uexküll's `Evidence type` column, 107/107 — the only place that separates *what kind* of evidence from *how strong* |\n| `strength_rationale` | free text, **separate field** | Uexküll glued rationale to enum with an em-dash (\"Strong — multiple independent examples\") producing ~100 values from a 3-value vocabulary. BCAP did the same with page numbers |\n| `provenance` | **enum + registry-resolved author slot (§6.4)** | `TEMPLATE:38-42`, 2,761 + 1,323 + 1,196 + 85 FAITHFUL keys in use |\n| `locus[]` | array of typed locator objects, min 1, **never a string** | As a free string it produced 17,287 cells in 10+ formats, 961 with no digit at all, 6,961 bare numbers with no declared numbering system |\n| `verbatim_ref` | `clause_id` + `insertion_anchor` | Dissertation's `insertion_anchor` is present on 235/235 cached verbatims and is the corpus's only content-addressed pointer that **still resolves today** |\n| `premises[]` | **ordered array** of `{premise_index, premise_text, ref}` | BCAP records enumerated premises with an explicit \"→ **conclusion**:\" step; BT carries premises 108/108. Both encode them as **one prose cell**, which is why nothing can traverse them |\n| `supports[]`, `supported_by[]` | arrays of `claim_id` | Dissertation puts **76% of 982 claims** into an explicit support graph with 841 typed edges. This answers \"every point of connection\" |\n| `contests[]`, `contested_by[]` | arrays of `claim_id` \\| `interlocutor_id` | Uncomfortable positions carry `contested_by`; BT carries **84 explicit claim-to-tension back-references** |\n| `tension_ids[]` | array | The same 84 refs + `contested-nodes.md`. Second half of \"every weakness\" |\n| `cites_primary[]`, `cites_secondary[]`, `implicit_citations_needed[]` | arrays of `{locus, tier, rationale}` | Dissertation `pCit`/`sCit`/`iCit` populated 982/982. **The third slot names the citation the prose is MISSING** — it is what makes the index an instrument, not a record |\n| `interlocutors[]` | `{interlocutor_id, role, locus}`, role **enum:** `anchor \\| corroborating \\| contested \\| superseded \\| background \\| methodological \\| definitional` | Uncomfortable's four loci concordances carry `role` on all 176 records; VDS carries `role` + `corpus_index_bridge` on 24 rows |\n| `coined_terms[]` | array of string | Dissertation `ct` (26 in DISS-03 alone) + its canonical-definition-site index — lets the index police the project's own vocabulary |\n| `flag_present`, `flag_text` | bool + the **quoted hedge** | Dissertation `fp` (128/156 in DISS-03) + `interpretive_flag_text` (\"'as I established in the preceding section'\"). Pairing them makes T3 auditable rather than asserted |\n| `disposition` | **enum:** `keep-verbatim \\| re-ground \\| enrich \\| supersede \\| drop` | VDS, 157/157 populated (re-ground 127, enrich 21, keep 7, supersede 2). The only forward-looking field in the corpus |\n| `analytic_anchor[]` | project enum (RODA: `A0-horizon, A1-perception, A2-phantasma, A3-doxa/emotion, A4-action/hexis, A4→A0′, union(R1–R7), recalcitrance, rupture, hinge, VR↔2D, framing`) | VDS: 12 values, ~240 attachments over 157 rows. Also the \"RODA locus\" column in every RDR2 beat-map. This is the corpus-wide generalisation of the concordance idea at `TEMPLATE:81-88` |\n| `volatility` | `{is_volatile, depends_on, resolved_at, resolution_note}` | VDS's `[V:…]` flags with in-place resolution stamps (\"hinge [resolved 2026-06-24: Part I §A₄ final · RODA v6]\"). Turns a vocabulary change into a work queue instead of silent rot |\n| `remediation` | `{action, corpus_index_candidates[], chroma_candidates[], external_query, effort}` | Dissertation `rem` 982/982, with real routing values (`RESOLVE_INLINENOTE+ADD_PRIMARY_CITATION`, `cCorp: ['corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/De Anima III.10']`) |\n| `use_scope` | **enum:** `index-only \\| citable-pending-<gate> \\| citable` | `BEX-ANCHOR:106-109` applied consent as an entry-wide ceiling; as a per-record field the 168-cell matrix is indexed now and quotable later |\n| `derivation` | **enum:** `agent-read \\| self-authored \\| inferred \\| script-derived` | `TEMPLATE:208-210` authorises orchestrator self-authoring with no marker; no record survives of which Boredom units were agent-built |\n| `confidence`, `needs_human_review` | `high/medium/low`, bool | BCAP already emits 30 `**Confidence**:` bullets; `****** UNVERIFIED:` is the de-facto review flag with no field to live in |\n| `build_provenance` | `{agent_id, model, retries, built_at, plan_sha}` | 26 defects trace to unrecoverable build history |\n| `schema_version` | string | Only Dissertation stamps one today |\n\n### 6.4 Controlled vocabularies — derived by union-and-dedup from actual use\n\n**`provenance`** — complete observed corpus-wide vocabulary with counts:\n`FE` 2,761 · `P/anticipatory-application` 1,323 · `burke-direct` 1,196 · `anticipatory-application` 524 · `INTERP-high` 380 · `INTERP-low` 368 · `calleja-direct` 180 · `FAITHFUL-<author>` 85 distinct keys (Slaby 175, Makransky 154, Parong 144, Richardson 132, Keane 130, Yakobi 108, Nacke 102, Tam 102, Seo 98, Kim 94, Holmqvist 88, Mansikka 86, …) · bracketed variants `[INTERP-high]` 276, `[INTERP-low]` 207, `[FE]` 43, `[P]` 33, `[INTERP-med]` 29, `[INTERP-medium]` 21, `[FE-STUDENT]` 12, `[FE-U]` 10.\n**Normalisations required:** merge `INTERP-med` ≡ `INTERP-medium`; merge bare `anticipatory-application` into `P/anticipatory-application`; strip brackets; **resolve `FAITHFUL-<author>` against a per-entry interlocutor registry** — the free-surname convention has already produced `FAITHFUL-B`, `FAITHFUL-C`, `FAITHFUL-DB`, `FAITHFUL-O`, `FAITHFUL-De`, `FAITHFUL-Tu`, and doubled forms (`FAITHFUL-Slaby` 175 vs `FAITHFUL-Slaby & Thonhauser` 8).\n**Closed set:** `FE | FE-U | FE-STUDENT | FE-TEACHER | FAITHFUL:<author_key> | P/anticipatory-application | INTERP-low | INTERP-med | INTERP-high | burke-direct | calleja-direct`.\n\n**`support_tier`** — adopted verbatim from `DISS-PIPE:333-341`, the only closed fully-populated tier vocabulary in the corpus. Observed distribution over 982 records: `T3-interpretive-but-flagged` 477 · `T1-textually-confirmed` 277 · `T2-textually-supported` 78 · `T5-under-supported` 71 · `T4-interpretive-but-unflagged` 41 · `T7-overreach` 22 · `T6-unsupported` 12 · `T8-secondary-needed` 4.\n**Migration crosswalk:** Uexküll `Strong` → T1/T2, `Moderate` → T3/T5, `Weak` → T6; BCAP \"Explicitly stated\"/\"Textually explicit\" → T1, `[INTERP-high] Heidegger's interpretive construction` → T3; VDS tier 1 → T1, tier 2 → T3.\n\n**`stance`** — union-and-dedup of Boredom's 170 free values and VR Pedagogy's, keeping every token that recurs:\n`asserts | defines | classifies | reports | extends | refines | qualifies | concedes | contests | refutes | restates | synthesizes | concludes | self-critiques | defers`.\n**Critical bug to design out:** Boredom has `stance: \"FE\"` **22 times**. `stance` and `provenance` must be separate required fields with **disjoint** enums, and the validator must reject cross-contamination. `null` illegal.\n\n**`evidence_type`** — collapsed from Uexküll's 105 distinct values:\n`textual-explicit | textual-inferred | philosophical-argument | empirical-experiment | empirical-observation | comparative | analogical | diagrammatic | statistical | anecdotal | authority-citation | methodological-principle`.\n\n**`relation`** — a versioned global registry file, seeded from the 645 observed values, with a reserved core set that may not be renamed and an `other` escape requiring `relation_raw` + a review flag. Entries may extend only by adding a subtype that declares its parent, written back to the registry **in the same commit**.\n\n### 6.5 The locator model, and graceful degradation\n\nA locator is a typed object, not a string. `locator_kind` is one of:\n\n| kind | fields | precision | proven by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `char-span` | `text_layer_id, char_start, char_end` | **clause** | NET-NEW; the sandbox achieves 93.0% (4,615/4,961) |\n| `bbox` | `doc_id, page_pdf, x0,y0,x1,y1` | **clause** | `archon evidence find --mode exact` already returns it |\n| `bekker` | `work, book, chapter, bekker_start, bekker_end` | **clause** | Aristotle: 2,323 loci **with line numbers**, 3,064 distinct line-anchored strings — an existing clause-level address system |\n| `timestamp` | `media_id, start_ms, end_ms, frame_id` | **sub-clause** | RDR2 Playthrough: 529 timestamps + 1,040 frame ids |\n| `line-range` | `text_layer_id, line_start, line_end` | near-clause | In-Game 995; Dissertation 982/982 |\n| `heidegger-h` | `h_page` | paragraph | `H.96`, `H.95–101` in BT prose |\n| `section` | `section_ref` | paragraph | `§21`, `§9b-β` |\n| `cell` | `subject, condition, item` | record | VLE / Boredom Experiment: 8 × 3 × 7 |\n| `page` | `page_printed, page_pdf` | **coarsest permitted** | `WENDT:129`, 307/307 |\n\n**Degradation rule.** Every claim carries **at least one** locator. `char-span` is **required** wherever the source has an extractable text layer. Degradation to a coarser kind requires an explicit `degradation_reason` from a closed enum (`ocr-only | scanned-image | no-text-layer | rights-withheld-span | media-source`), and the entry's gate report must publish the **span-coverage rate** with a floor of 0.90. A `page`-only locator without a `degradation_reason` is a validation failure. Every locator resolves through the source's declared `page_offset_map`, and ≥5 sampled loci per source must round-trip by exact string match.\n\n### 6.6 Worked example\n\n**Source record as it exists today** — `corpus/index/VR Pedagogy Secondary (Part III)/Biocca Burgoon & Harms - Robust Theory of Social Presence (2003)/ped-sec-29-…-robust-theory.md:7`, the sentence that carries the fabricated quotation, plus the `-edges.csv` row it produced:\n\n```\nped-sec-29, treats-construct, presence (spatial/physical), p.456-457,\n  \"spatial/telepresence = sense of being in the place (FE, p.456-457)\"\n```\n\nTotal addressable structure: one CSV row, one page range, one 6-word quoted string that **occurs nowhere in the source**, tagged as the source's own published claim, undetectable by all fourteen gates.\n\n**The same material in the proposed schema:**\n\n```jsonc\n// CLAUSE — the addressable span, stored regardless of display rights\n{\n  \"clause_id\": \"PEDSEC29-CL00184\",\n  \"doc_id\": \"sha256:4f1c…9ab2\",                    // NOT a path (In-Game lesson)\n  \"edition_key\": \"Presence 12(5), 2003, pp.456-480\",\n  \"text_layer_id\": \"pdftotext-24.02.0 --layout -enc UTF-8 :: sha256:7d0e…c114\",\n  \"char_start\": 18244, \"char_end\": 18291,\n  \"sentence_index\": 412,\n  \"line_start\": 40, \"line_end\": 41,\n  \"page_pdf\": 12, \"page_printed\": 456,\n  \"citation_address\": {\"kind\": \"page\", \"page_printed\": 456},\n  \"quote\": \"the sense of \\\"being in the virtual place\\\"\",\n  \"quote_sha256\": \"sha256:a91f…30dd\",\n  \"quote_word_count\": 7,\n  \"normalized_quote\": \"the sense of being in the virtual place\",\n  \"rights_tier\": \"third-party-copyright\",\n  \"redact_on_render\": true,                        // storage ≠ display\n  \"bbox\": [72.0, 331.4, 388.6, 344.1],\n  \"extraction_probe\": {\"ligature_ok\": true, \"diacritic_ok\": true, \"words_per_page\": 612}\n}\n\n// CLAIM\n{\n  \"claim_id\": \"PEDSEC-29-C0037\",\n  \"entry_id\": \"vr-pedagogy-secondary\", \"unit_id\": \"ped-sec-29\",\n  \"claim_text\": \"Biocca, Burgoon and Harms distinguish spatial/telepresence — the sense of being in the virtual place — from social presence.\",\n  \"clause_refs\": [\"PEDSEC29-CL00184\", \"PEDSEC29-CL00187\"],\n  \"claim_kind\": \"definition\",\n  \"scope\": \"section-thesis\",\n  \"stance\": \"defines\",\n  \"support_tier\": \"T1-textually-confirmed\",\n  \"evidence_type\": \"textual-explicit\",\n  \"strength_rationale\": \"Definitional sentence in the review's terminology section; restated at p.457.\",\n  \"provenance\": \"FE\",\n  \"locus\": [{\"kind\": \"char-span\", \"text_layer_id\": \"…c114\", \"char_start\": 18244, \"char_end\": 18291},\n            {\"kind\": \"page\", \"page_printed\": 456, \"page_pdf\": 12}],\n  \"verbatim_ref\": {\"clause_id\": \"PEDSEC29-CL00184\",\n                   \"insertion_anchor\": \"distinguishes spatial from social presence\"},\n  \"premises\": [],\n  \"supports\": [\"PEDSEC-29-C0041\"],\n  \"supported_by\": [],\n  \"contests\": [], \"contested_by\": [\"PEDSEC-07-C0112\"],\n  \"tension_ids\": [\"VRPED-T-004\"],\n  \"cites_primary\": [], \n  \"cites_secondary\": [{\"locus\": {\"kind\":\"page\",\"page_printed\":456},\n                       \"tier\": \"T1-textually-confirmed\", \"rationale\": \"cites Short et al. 1976\"}],\n  \"implicit_citations_needed\": [],\n  \"interlocutors\": [{\"interlocutor_id\": \"VRPED-I-SHORT-1976\", \"role\": \"superseded\",\n                     \"locus\": {\"kind\":\"page\",\"page_printed\":456}}],\n  \"coined_terms\": [],\n  \"flag_present\": false, \"flag_text\": null,\n  \"disposition\": \"keep-verbatim\",\n  \"analytic_anchor\": [\"A1-perception\"],\n  \"volatility\": {\"is_volatile\": false},\n  \"remediation\": {\"action\": \"NONE\", \"effort\": \"none\"},\n  \"use_scope\": \"citable\",\n  \"derivation\": \"agent-read\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\", \"needs_human_review\": false,\n  \"build_provenance\": {\"agent_id\": \"phase2-ped-sec-29\", \"model\": \"…\", \"retries\": 0,\n                       \"built_at\": \"…\", \"plan_sha\": \"…\"},\n  \"schema_version\": \"index-claim-v1.0\"\n}\n```\n\n**What this buys, concretely:** `check-quotes.py` re-slices `text_layer_id[18244:18291]`, compares to `quote_sha256`, and the **fabrication fails the build**. `redact_on_render: true` means the clause is stored and verifiable while never rendered at length. `support_tier: T1` is machine-separable from the entry's 117 P-tagged speculations. `contested_by` makes the weakness queryable. And one source that previously produced ~38 CSV rows now produces 50–500 such records, at the Dissertation's proven ~1-per-58-words density.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Requirements for the new entry-creation plan\n\nNumbered, exhaustive, grouped. Every requirement names its motivating evidence. **This section is the direct input to writing the plan.**\n\n### A. Source preparation\n\n**A1.** Derive the source inventory **from disk** in Phase 0 — `md5sum`, `pdfinfo`, first-page title/author/year/venue extraction — and **diff it against any plan-supplied table**, reporting phantoms and extras as blocking findings before any unit is assigned. *Evidence: `BOR-SEC:44-85` produced a nonexistent \"Standish 2015\" (a mislabeled Mertel duplicate) costing a build-abort cycle, a reversed byline, and two omitted Elpidorou 2018 files that were the sole grounding for the plan's own debate axis.*\n\n**A2.** Every factual assertion the plan makes about a file (page count, identity, uniqueness, authorship, year) carries its **verification command and output inline**, or is marked UNVERIFIED and assigned to Phase 0. *Evidence: `BOR-SEC:92` asserted a 727-page proceedings volume was \"the single extracted paper.\"*\n\n**A3.** Preserve the de-dup/haystack rubric verbatim (`TEMPLATE:57-67`) and persist every disposition with its md5 into the manifest. *Evidence: 49 files → 44 units with two real salvages; 23 duplicate groups across 288 corpus PDFs.*\n\n**A4.** Add a **source-admissibility precondition**: text-layer sanity (distinct per-page text hashes, extracted-words-per-page floor), ligature integrity probe for the pypdfium2 fi/ff/fl dropout, diacritic probe for the source's language, and citation completeness (author, venue, year, pagination anchor). Record `text_quality`; **quarantine** failures with a remediation task rather than authoring around them. *Evidence: `ptf-01` shipped with identical `text_hash` on all 11 pages and all verbatims UNVERIFIED; `riv-02` shipped with an unverified venue; `ig-10-deep.json:425-430` documents hand-repairing `difﬁ culty`/`sufﬁ cient`/`ﬁ gurative`.*\n\n**A5.** Declare `RIGHTS_TIER` **per source** (`own-work | public-domain | licensed | third-party-copyright`) in the source manifest record. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:44` hardcodes one assumption for a template meant to process \"ANY folder\"; the corpus spans the user's own thesis, Aristotle, Equiano 1789, Radcliffe 1794 and in-copyright monographs.*\n\n**A6.** Declare an **ENTRY PROFILE** before building, from a fixed set with different floors and required artifacts: `PRIMARY-DATASET` · `MONOGRAPH` · `ARTICLE-CLUSTER` · `SMALL-PAIR (N≤3)` · `OWN-PROSE`. Record it in the manifest; select gate thresholds from it. *Evidence: a 2-source rhetoric pair, a 4-source theory cluster and a 92 GB instrumented dataset all converged on the same 7–10-node ontology-only shape.*\n\n**A7.** Reserve the entry's id **prefix** in a committed registry (prefix → entry → grammar → allocated ranges → status) as step 0. *Evidence: the `bor-` → `bex-` rename was unrecorded and `bor-` was subsequently taken by Boredom Secondary.*\n\n### B. Extraction and addressing\n\n**B1.** **Commit the normalized full text as an immutable entry artifact**: `<entry>/_source/<source_id>.txt` plus a sidecar `{extractor, extractor_version, exact_command, flags, source_sha256, text_sha256, extracted_at, page_offset_map}`. **Forbid scratchpad destinations.** *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:137-140`, `VR-PED:166-171` (which observes the scratchpad does not persist and specifies it anyway); ~1,000 In-Game clause pointers dead.*\n\n**B2.** Every locator names its `text_layer_id`. **Gate:** every referenced text artifact exists and its `sha256` matches. *Evidence: one deterministic re-extraction under this rule resurrects ~1,000 In-Game clause pointers in a single step.*\n\n**B3.** **Mandatory locator calibration per source before extraction:** sample ≥5 (recommended ≥10) pages spread across the document, record `(page_pdf, page_printed)` pairs, assert the mapping is affine and constant, check monotonicity, and record a **piecewise map** when it is not. Store in the source record. *Evidence: Aristotle 33/34 records wrong by up to 47 pages and 101/188 Bekker loci off by >2; `rickert-structured/manifest.json:7` declares 20 and drifts to 15. Model the good pattern: `Uncomfortable .../us-literary-loci-concordance.json` `page_offset_rule`.*\n\n**B4.** **Gate:** every recorded locus resolves through the declared map into the document's real page/char range, and ≥3 randomly sampled loci per source are verified by **exact string match** on the mapped page.\n\n**B5.** Record `char_start`/`char_end` on **every** clause in a source with an extractable text layer. Degradation to a coarser locator requires a `degradation_reason` from a closed enum. **Gate:** span-coverage rate ≥ 0.90. *Evidence: the sandbox already achieves 93.0% (4,615/4,961); the whole built corpus achieves 0%.*\n\n**B6.** **Persist retrieval provenance, never assert it.** Every quotation record stores `{doc_id, chunk_id, page, bbox[4], char_span, sim, mode, snapshot_id, run_timestamp}` exactly as `archon evidence find --mode exact` returns them. **Ban the token `bbox ✓` as evidence.** *Evidence: 45+ ticks, zero coordinates — a discarded address system.*\n\n**B7.** Apply **UTF-8 NFC normalisation**, one canonical orthography per lemma with `variants[]`, and a checker flagging any two lemmas differing only by normalisation or mojibake. **Forbid encoding fallbacks in the loader** — a decode failure is a hard error. *Evidence: `compile-corpus-index.py:157-163` silently falls back to latin-1; Uexküll ships four orthographies and `Wohnhulle` is the one that compiles.*\n\n**B8.** Treat **Bekker line pairs and media timestamps as first-class clause-address subtypes** with typed slots and resolvers, not prose. *Evidence: Aristotle already records 2,323 Bekker loci with line numbers; RDR2 Playthrough already records 529 timestamps and 1,040 frame ids — both already at or below clause level.*\n\n### C. Schema and IDs\n\n**C1.** **Ship machine-checkable JSON Schema files as artifacts of the plan**, referenced by path: `claim.schema.json`, `clause.schema.json`, `edge.schema.json`, `locus.schema.json`, `tension.schema.json`, `term.schema.json`. Plus **one fully-worked exemplar record per type**. *Evidence: \"schema\" appears 0× in `TEMPLATE` and 0× in `BOR-SEC`; no `*.schema.json` exists in the repo (verified); 49 schema-violation defects.*\n\n**C2.** **The CLAIM is the unit of production** (§6.3); the unit `.md` is demoted to an optional rendering **generated** from records. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:152-165` makes the source the atom; 7 records/source vs 50–500 target.*\n\n**C3.** **The CLAUSE is a separate record** (§6.2) referenced by `clause_id`, not nested inside claims.\n\n**C4.** **Forbid bare strings in any array.** *Evidence: 87 bare-string `concepts[]`, 146 bare `interlocutors[]`, 57 bare `sections[]`, 46 bare `tensions[]`.*\n\n**C5.** Fix the case convention (**snake_case**) in the schema, not in prose. *Evidence: `sampleN`/`keyResult` ×45 vs `sample_n`/`key_result` ×38 inside one field set.*\n\n**C6.** **Full id grammar at every level, with worked examples**, globally unique across the whole `corpus/index` tree: `<ENTRY>-<UNIT>-C<nnnn>` claims, `-S<nnn>` sections, `-T<nnn>` tensions, `-Q<nnn>` quotes, `<DOC>-CL<nnnnn>` clauses, `<UNIT>-e<nnn>` edges. **Explicitly forbid unprefixed local counters.** *Evidence: 37 colliding `C1..C22`/`F1..F8`; Wendt 20 collisions; two disjoint registries in one Uncomfortable directory.*\n\n**C7.** Ids are **content-addressed and stable across rebuilds** (`entry + unit + sha256(claim_text)[0:8]`), never positional. *Evidence: `MIGRATION:64`'s `{unit}-c{n}` renumbers on every insert — the mechanism behind 44 dangling-reference and 10 id-collision defects.*\n\n**C8.** **Ids are the only join key.** Name collisions across entries become an explicit authored `sameAs` edge, never an automatic merge. **Gate:** id uniqueness within the entry and a cross-entry collision report. *Evidence: the compiler merges by `name.lower()` (`:1310-1349`), producing 20 fused rows with concatenated provenance and no ids at all.*\n\n**C9.** Every node and record carries a **stable machine id distinct from its display label**; all cross-file references use the id. If a target parser format cannot hold an id, **extend the parser in the same plan and show the diff**. *Evidence: 68 Boredom nodes with no id; 508 back-references keyed on strings that already disagree (\"EEG eyes-open vs eyes-closed\" vs \"…versus eyes-closed baseline\").*\n\n**C10.** **Every typed field gets a closed enum stated inline in the plan** (§6.4), with `null` illegal on `stance`, `support_tier` and `provenance`. Any out-of-vocabulary value goes to a per-entry vocabulary-extension file with a one-line justification — **never inlined**. *Evidence: 162 stance values / 195 nulls / 108 hapax.*\n\n**C11.** **Separate every enum from its prose.** `stance` and `provenance` are disjoint enums and the validator rejects cross-contamination; `strength` and `strength_rationale` are separate fields. *Evidence: `stance: \"FE\"` ×22; `\"Strong — multiple independent examples\"` producing ~100 values from a 3-value vocabulary; `\"Textually explicit (pp. 33, 40, 43)\"`.*\n\n**C12.** Preserve the source's own wording as a first-class field (`surface_form`) alongside the normalized label. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:81-88` normalizes to ≤15 labels and pushes the source's term into an unschematised note.*\n\n**C13.** **Stamp `schema_version` into every artifact.** *Evidence: only Dissertation does; nothing else can be safely migrated.*\n\n**C14.** **Cap every free-text field at a character limit** (~1,200) in the schema, and fail any record whose prose field contains more than one page anchor. *Evidence: `us-03-radcliffe.json:102` carries an 8,000-word `outline` blob; page anchors buried in prose are unaddressable.*\n\n**C15.** **Ship a global, versioned relation-and-type registry** as a plan artifact. Entries extend it only by adding a registered subtype declaring its parent, written back in the same commit. **Gate:** every relation string resolves. *Evidence: 645 relation values, 47 CSV dialects; no cross-entry union possible.*\n\n**C16.** **One concept registry per entry.** **Gate:** id-space disjointness. *Evidence: Uncomfortable's `C-US-01..40` vs `US-C-001..036` with zero overlap.*\n\n**C17.** **One source of truth per fact.** Author the machine-readable form as canonical and **generate** every `.md` rendering by committed script; gate on byte-reproducibility. **Never mandate two hand-authored twins.** *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:114,:176-177`; 36 canonical positions lost to `.json` twins the compiler never opens.*\n\n**C18.** Decouple **storage handles from bibliographic facts**: folders and filenames use the opaque id alone; author/year/title live in the manifest as data. *Evidence: `ped-sec-14`'s folder is permanently `Colin et al. …` while its 30 provenance tags read `FAITHFUL-Barrett et al.`*\n\n**C19.** **Forbid parenthetical qualifiers in any identifier reaching an addressable slot.** State the heading grammar as a testable production: `#### <int>. <Name>` where `Name` matches `^[^()]+$`; qualifiers move to an explicit bullet; aliases are declared, never derived. *Evidence: `VR-PED:118-127` + `:186-187` + `compile-corpus-index.py:687,:734-736` = 19 corrupted nodes and `technological`/`control` corpus-wide.*\n\n**C20.** **Canonical-term admission gate:** a term enters the global greedy-match list only if declared in a per-entry terms file, above a minimum length, and not a bare common English word (stoplist). Print the **full diff** of terms this entry adds, for sign-off. *Evidence: 1,722 entries including whole sentences (\"Debate axis 9: social presence reliably predicts…\") and the bare words `technological`, `Presence`, `control`.*\n\n### D. Provenance and verification\n\n**D1.** **Promote the three-tag provenance vocabulary to a required, closed, validated field** (§6.4), normalising `INTERP-med`≡`INTERP-medium`, bare `anticipatory-application`, and bracket variants, with `FAITHFUL:<author_key>` resolving against a per-entry interlocutor registry. *Evidence: 85 free-surname keys including `FAITHFUL-B`, `FAITHFUL-DB`, and doubled forms.*\n\n**D2.** **Adopt the 8-tier support taxonomy verbatim** (`DISS-PIPE:333-341`) with its remediation action per tier. *Evidence: 982 records; T4/T5/T6/T7 are \"every weakness\", machine-selectable.*\n\n**D3.** **Make quotation machine-verified, not length-limited.** Store `{quote_id, source_doc, char_start, char_end, exact_text, sha256}`; interpolate quotes into prose **only by quote_id** (wire the existing `scripts/substitute-quote-ids.py`); gate byte equality against the committed source on every build. *Evidence: the `ped-sec-29` fabrication — 6 words, inside the 12-word allowance, tagged FE, undetectable by all fourteen gates.*\n\n**D4.** **Ban quotation marks in hand-typed prose.**\n\n**D5.** **Forbid the `FE` tag on any sentence containing a quoted span lacking a verified `quote_id`.**\n\n**D6.** **Replace the blanket 25-word ban with a rights-tiered storage/display split** (A5): store the exact span for **every** tier as internal evidence with `redact_on_render`; apply word ceilings only to **rendered** output and only for restricted tiers. State the policy explicitly: **a claim/clause index requires the clause**, so the suppression practised at `ig-10-deep.json:434-441` and `us-03-radcliffe.json:110,:234` is incompatible with the goal. *Evidence: zero spans in 1,758 files; definitions truncated to exactly 24 words to clear a ceiling.*\n\n**D7.** **Mandatory bibliographic verification in Phase 1** against the title page and DOI/copyright line, recording the **version-of-record** year. **Gate:** every unit has `verified_bibliography: true`. *Evidence: `ped-sec-14` surname; three unresolved year errors and one mis-linkage in `citation-corrections-2026-07-16.md`, unapplied per its line 52.*\n\n**D8.** **Gate:** no unresolved corrections file and no unresolved verification marker may exist at ship time. *Evidence: 6 of 55 Boredom manifest records carry `year: null`; `bor-sec-11` still carries \"(author verification needed)\"; a deferred folder rename was never executed.*\n\n**D9.** **Require a `derivation` field on every record** (`agent-read | self-authored | inferred | script-derived`) and **gate on the self-authored fraction**. Record per-unit build provenance (agent id, model, retries, plan sha). *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:208-210`; no record survives of which units were orchestrator-invented.*\n\n**D10.** **Require an independent second-reader verification pass** on a stated sample fraction with a stated pass threshold, performed by a different agent than the author. *Evidence: producer and judge are currently the same agent for every gate.*\n\n**D11.** **Never name a checker the plan does not ship** (§H). *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:198,:228`, `VR-PED:204,:223`, `BEX-ANCHOR:182` all name a verbatim detector that does not exist.*\n\n**D12.** **Cite compiler behaviour by function name plus a reproduction command**, never by line number, and require the executing agent to run it and paste the output. *Evidence: `BEX-ANCHOR` cites \"verified `compile-corpus-index.py` L1197–1207\" — wrong branch, fallback direction stated backwards.*\n\n**D13.** **Split PII rules from verification rules.** (1) No participant name in any tracked artifact or committed script, grep-enforced. (2) Transcript hygiene via a **committed name-blind enumerator** emitting only codes, hashes and counts. **Explicitly forbid any gate that blocks verification of the artifact itself.** *Evidence: `BEX-ANCHOR:101-105` forbade the inspection that would have caught the fabricated `ch-obs` fact; `scripts/boredom-o9/common.py` proves full processing and PII discipline are compatible.*\n\n**D14.** **Model consent as a per-record `use_scope` field, never as an entry-wide content ceiling.** *Evidence: `BEX-ANCHOR:106-109` capped a 168-record matrix at ~8 assertions.*\n\n### E. Edges and connection\n\n**E1.** **One canonical edge record, one physical format** at per-source and aggregate level: `{edge_id, entry_id, subject_id, relation (registry-resolved), object_id, locator[] (a SET), provenance, support_tier, deriving_unit, note}`. Provide the header line **verbatim** in the plan; gate on exact header equality after BOM/CRLF normalisation. *Evidence: four sibling clusters shipped four headers; 47 dialects corpus-wide.*\n\n**E2.** `subject_id`/`object_id` must be **resolvable ids from declared namespaces**. **Gate:** referential integrity — any unresolvable endpoint fails the build. *Evidence: 119 rows with `§4`/`n.8`/`Intro` as subject; `grounds-measure` 0/37 resolved.*\n\n**E3.** **For every cross-entry relation, carry the literal target id list inline in the plan** (as `BOR-SEC:24` does), or a command that generates it. Where the target entry does not exist, require a **reserved-namespace placeholder id** (`bex-TBD-eeg-fa`), never free text. *Evidence: enumerated 68/68 vs unenumerated 0/37 and 0/128.*\n\n**E4.** **Forbid authoring any edge whose target entry does not exist.** Route intent to `pending-bridges.json` that a later build resolves. *Evidence: `VR-PED:20,:132` authorised edges to an anchor it flagged NOT YET BUILT; 24 were later retired wholesale; 44 dangling-reference defects.*\n\n**E5.** **Never dedupe on content.** The global store is a concatenation keyed on `edge_id`; near-duplicate detection produces a **report** a human resolves. **Gate:** `count(global) == Σ count(per-unit)` as exact equality. *Evidence: Boredom lost 18 locus-distinct rows, VR-Ped lost 2 note-distinct rows, from the same instruction.*\n\n**E6.** If any merge occurs, it **unions locator sets** and emits a reconciliation record `{inputs_n, outputs_n, dropped_n, drop_reason_histogram, dropped_ids[]}`. **Gate:** `dropped_n == Σ histogram`, and any `drop_reason: unknown` fails the build. Report `loci_preserved` vs `loci_in`.\n\n**E7.** **Floor the source-derived records and CAP the interpretive ones** (`P`-tagged ≤ 0.15 × (FE + FAITHFUL)). *Evidence: `VR-PED:184,:220` mandate a **minimum** of our own speculation per unit; 117 P-tagged edges = 10.4% of the store.*\n\n**E8.** **Separate the data cap from the render cap, explicitly.** No cap on cross-entry edges, canonical nodes, concordance cells or claim records in the store; caps apply only to a generated view, produced by filtering on tier/centrality. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:182-185`'s ≤25 cap forced strand-level aggregation that reduced 117 unit-level bridges to integer labels.*\n\n**E9.** **The concordance (and every matrix) is a GENERATED VIEW over claim records**, never authored, never join-built. Every cell-source assertion resolves to exactly one `claim_id` and carries page/span, direction, effect size or null, and provenance. **Gate:** `unbacked_assertions == 0`. **Explicitly forbid mechanical co-occurrence derivation by name.** *Evidence: 316 of 348 assertions (90.8%) unbacked; 0/91 and 0/94 cells carry the mandated locus and note.*\n\n**E10.** **Build a reverse-reference index at compile time** (record id → every file citing it) and make correction **transactional**: changing a record lists all dependents and fails until each is updated or waived. *Evidence: a superseded VLE figure left 12 stale live copies in a sibling entry plus 4 `global-edges.csv` rows.*\n\n**E11.** **The bridge selector must reject empty endpoints before scoring, and omit the block entirely when nothing scores.** Never label an `INTERP-` tagged record \"verified\". *Evidence: `cross-author-utils.ts:473-474` makes `t.includes('')` always true; 4 of 6 simulated topics render `<-> ? ()` under a MUST-cite directive; 525 of 552 candidates wasted, 85% \"unrelated\"; well-formed anchors returned 25 of 27 usable — a **6× yield difference**.*\n\n**E12.** **Gate anchor validity to 1.00 before any derivative generation**, and report anchor **coverage** (only 8 of 72 hooks were ever exercised).\n\n### F. Weakness and tension encoding\n\n**F1.** **Tension is a first-class record with a stated schema** covering all eight shapes on disk: `{tension_id, entry_id, endpoint_a{node_id,label}, endpoint_b{node_id,label}, relation, directed, evidence_locus_a, evidence_locus_b, description, unit_ids[], claim_ids[]}`. Must subsume `node_a/node_b`, `nodeA/nodeB/type`, `wendt_position/against`, `pole_A/pole_B`, `tension_id/label/supporting_units`, `pentad_terms_involved`, and the FCM `locus_a/locus_b` variant. *Evidence: 4 of 11 files yield zero; `MIGRATION:73-81`'s superset covers 1 of the 4 broken shapes.*\n\n**F2.** **Name `tension-edges.json` explicitly in the folder layout with its exact compiler-required keys, quoting the parsing function.** **Gate:** `compiled-index.json` tensionEdges for this entry `> 0`. *Evidence: the string appears 0× in every plan; Boredom's 211 tensions and 11 debate axes contribute 0 of 64.*\n\n**F3.** **Make negative claims a first-class record type** (`claim_kind: negative`) with a locus scope, replacing the prose \"Not treated:\" line. *Evidence: `bor-sec-30` names 8 explicitly-absent measures and `bor-sec-13` 3 absent constructs — in prose, in no JSON.*\n\n**F4.** **Replace count targets on relational discoveries with coverage + evidence gates.** Every recorded disagreement must cite ≥2 distinct records with resolvable loci on opposing sides, and carry a boolean `staged_by_sources`. Report constructed axes separately; **never gate on the total**. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:219`'s 8–12 band; VR-Ped `DA-07`/`DA-08` cite one unit each; Boredom flags 3 of 11 as `constructedByCluster`.*\n\n**F5.** **Re-base contested readings on named external interlocutors** and give them a typed record schema. *Evidence (adjudicated §2.4): VR-Ped `CR-01`/`CR-03` contest Short et al. 1976 and the SSQ, neither a cluster unit — so this survives at N=1; but 18 shipped against a stated 8–12 because `contested-readings.md` has no format.*\n\n**F6.** **Carry `contested_by[]`, `tension_ids[]`, `support_tier` T4–T7, `implicit_citations_needed[]` and `volatility` as the five machine-queryable weakness channels.** *Evidence: BT's 84 claim-to-tension back-references and `contested-nodes.md` are the corpus's only working weakness graph; Dissertation's `iCit` is the only field that names a **missing** citation; VDS's `[V:…]` flags are the only defence against silent vocabulary rot.*\n\n### G. Gates\n\n**G1.** **Every gate is a named executable with a numeric threshold and an exit code**, collected in a committed per-entry gate script. Named checkers the plan must ship **before authoring begins**: `check-schema.py`, `check-ids.py`, `check-loci.py`, `check-projection.py`, `check-density.py`, `check-coverage.py`, `check-registration.py`, `check-quotes.py`, `check-lemmas.py`, `check-mermaid.sh`, `check-debates.py`, `check-reachability.py`, `emit-gates.py`. **A gate whose executable is missing FAILS; it does not pass by narration.**\n\n**G2.** **Mandatory `_synthesis/gates.json` + `metrics.json` per entry**, written by the checker and **never by an authoring agent**: `{gate_id, scope, statement, threshold_expr, threshold_value, measured, verdict (PASS|FAIL|SKIPPED-N1|N/A-by-construction), checker, checker_version, measured_at, input_sha256, evidence_path}` plus an aggregate exit code. Registration is conditional on zero failures. *Evidence: 2 of 27 entries have any gate report; 1 has metrics.*\n\n**G3.** **Never write a derived constant into a gate.** Every threshold is an expression over a machine-read value (`12 * manifest.totalAnalyticalUnits`), and the manifest is regenerated from disk. *Evidence: `VR-PED:213,:216` froze N=23 while the manifest says 34; `BOR-SEC:258`'s \"~44\" passed at 55.*\n\n**G4.** **Add a SCOPE-CHANGE PROCEDURE** and remove \"do not re-open\" phrasing from any decision a later phase can invalidate: any change to N re-runs the gate script and requires fresh sign-off. *Evidence: `VR-PED:226`.*\n\n**G5.** **Replace \"compiler runs clean\" with validate-then-load that exits non-zero.** Required assertions: manifest-declared record count per source == loaded count; **zero-yield for a registered source is a hard failure**; every rejected record is written to a rejects file with a reason; **gate on the rejects file being empty**. Require the compiler to emit a discard report; define clean as `exit 0 AND discarded == 0`. *Evidence: `main()` always returns 0; zero `warn()` calls while discarding 55 records.*\n\n**G6.** **Gate on REACHABILITY with a hard number:** `reachable_records / authored_records ≥ 0.95`, computed by a script that loads the compiled index and edge store and resolves authored ids. Require `_synthesis/reachability.json` declaring which files are runtime inputs and which are human-only. **No artifact may ship at 0% reachability without a signed waiver naming the future loader.** *Evidence: Boredom 2.3%, VR-Ped ≈1%, Boredom Experiment 8 of 9 files at 0%.*\n\n**G7.** **Per-layer non-zero contribution assertion:** for every layer the entry authors, read the compiled artifact back and assert `compiled_count[layer][entry] > 0`. *This one check catches every zero-yield tension file, every unparsable ontology, every unregistered entry.*\n\n**G8.** **A REGISTRATION CONTRACT TEST as a Phase-0 gate**, before any authoring: compile a committed fixture and assert the output **exactly equals** an expected node list. Re-run at G1 on the real entry asserting (a) compiled count == authored count, (b) every compiled name string-equals its authored heading, (c) `greek`/`transliteration` are empty for non-classical entries, (d) `canonicalTerms` contributed minus authored names == ∅. *Evidence: a count gate certified 60 nodes as success while 19 were corrupted.*\n\n**G9.** **Density is the primary volume gate**, expressed per source: `records_per_1000_source_words`, with the band declared by profile and calibrated from the two proven exemplars (Dissertation ~1 per 58 words; VDS ~1 per 59 words; sandbox 155–512 claims/article). **Delete all prose word-count targets.** *Evidence: 8.4 readings/unit at one record per 1,009 source words; 17 of 18 band violations were overshoots.*\n\n**G10.** **Add a distribution gate:** no unit below 50% of the entry median claims/page. *Evidence: three Boredom units shipped zero readings and passed; Holmqvist 0.19/page vs Aho 1.67/page.*\n\n**G11.** **Per-source coverage gate:** publish the source's section/page inventory as a Phase-1 artifact, then gate `sections_with_≥1_claim / total_sections` and `pages_with_≥1_locus / total_pages`. *Evidence: nothing prevents an entry from covering only the abstract; the model is `BEX-v1:259-260`'s 24-cell \"no silent gaps\" rule with a computable denominator.*\n\n**G12.** **Replace file-existence completeness with content-predicate completeness**, validated per unit **immediately on agent return**: schema-validate, assert record floors, assert enum membership, assert every `quote_id` verifies, assert no placeholder strings. **Re-dispatch failures to a fresh agent WITH the source; never let the orchestrator self-author a unit it has not read.** *Evidence: 34/34 and 55/55 trios existed and 36 defects shipped inside them.*\n\n**G13.** **Define N=1 behaviour explicitly for every gate.** Per-source intrinsic gates (all meaningful at N=1): records per 1,000 source words · span-resolution rate 1.0 · quote-verification rate 1.0 · enum-conformance 1.0 · schema-validity 1.0 · locator-resolution 1.0 · `unbacked_assertions == 0` · `dangling_refs == 0` · `duplicate_ids == 0` · reachability ≥ 0.95 · section coverage · self-authored fraction. **Only three gates move to an optional GROUP layer with `N/A-by-construction`:** documented debates, intra-cluster citation network, scholarly-evolution arc (§3.2). **Do not** move the concordance, contested readings, concept extraction or the edge floor — the adjudication shows they survive at N=1.\n\n**G14.** **Scope-tag every deliverable and every gate** as RECORD / ENTRY / GROUP with a declared minimum N; the checker emits `N/A-by-construction` rather than a missing artifact below the minimum, and **skipping is a pass**.\n\n**G15.** **Preserve the \"Gates NOT fully met (reported honestly)\" section as a REQUIRED section** of the gates report. *Evidence: RDR2's candour is the reason its shortfall is knowable at all.*\n\n**G16.** **Separate producer from judge structurally.** Authoring agents may not write gate results. G1 reviews `gates.json`, the per-layer compiled-contribution delta, a **checker-selected random sample** of k records with their loci actually opened and resolved, and the unresolved-debt list. *Evidence: G1 currently inspects one author-chosen trio — 1.8% of a 55-unit build; every extant gate verdict is embedded in the artifact it judges.*\n\n**G17.** **Name the exact backup paths and assert their existence and timestamp ordering.** *Evidence: `BOR-SEC:243` names two files that are absent from the entry's `.backups/`.*\n\n**G18.** **Name the renderer and require its output as a committed artifact**, or drop the graph gate. `mmdc` v11.14.0 **is** installed (verified). Prefer: generate `.mmd` from records by script, as views. *Evidence: 2 of 15 `.mmd`-bearing entries have any render record; RDR2 deferred on a false premise.*\n\n**G19.** **Mandatory post-build corpus-wide consistency sweep as a gate:** after any entry is created or renamed, grep the whole index for assertions about its prior state (`not yet built`, `****** UNVERIFIED`, superseded prefixes, superseded counts) and **fail on any hit**. *Evidence: 22 live hits for the Boredom anchor; 12 for the superseded VLE figure.*\n\n**G20.** **Ban derived numerals from the runtime-reachable ontology file.** Node definitions reference record ids; every figure is generated at build time. **Gate:** no numeral in the ontology file lacks a record-id provenance. *Evidence: 7 of 18 VLE nodes are stale and are 100% of what VLE serves to runtime.*\n\n### H. Orchestration\n\n**H1.** **Preserve G0 and G1 with the no-commit rule and mandatory timestamped backups** (`TEMPLATE:100-103`, `:189`, `:200-201`, `:229`), changing only *what* G1 is shown (G16).\n\n**H2.** **Move registration to entry CREATION, not Phase 5.** A stub entry registers on day one and grows; an unfinished entry is visible-and-empty, never invisible. *Evidence: 8 of 27 entries unregistered because registration was the terminal step; 685 files (39%) invisible.*\n\n**H3.** **Specify sharded, deterministic, idempotent aggregation.** Per-source records are complete and valid independently; **all aggregation is performed by a committed re-runnable script, not a model**; model-authored synthesis operates over the script's output, sharded by axis with a declared merge order; the aggregation is re-run from scratch at the end and **byte-compared** to the committed artifact. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:167` main-loop authoring already produced a locus-blind dedup and a 162-value vocabulary at 2,924 sub-items; at claim level a 55-source cluster is 5,000–27,500 records.*\n\n**H4.** **Formalise `manifest.planCorrections`** with a fixed schema `{issue, files, evidence[] (commands + outputs), resolution, residual}`, and require the executing agent to record contradictions **without editing the plan**. Extend it to schema deviations. *Evidence: Boredom's 7 corrections, especially #7.*\n\n**H5.** **Keep no-stall, but make every deferral a typed record:** `_audit/deferred.json` `{deferral_id, what, blocking_dependency, unblock_condition, owner, review_date, resolution_procedure, on_clear_actions[exact files to rewrite], created_at}`. **Gate:** fail any entry whose deferral references a dependency that now exists. Add a corpus-wide sweep whenever a new entry lands. **Gate entry status on the open-items file being empty.** *Evidence: 37 + 12 + 3 markers unresolved 13 days after the blocker cleared; a p=0.008 finding never entered the index.*\n\n**H6.** **Preserve \"refuse and escalate\" as a sanctioned agent outcome.** *Evidence: the `bor-sec-18` refusal.*\n\n**H7.** **Require the manifest to be REGENERATED from disk at the end of every phase**, with the hand-authored table kept as `declared` beside a script-produced `discovered` block. **Gate:** `declared == discovered`, both directions, exact. **Every count stated anywhere in the entry is script-emitted, never typed.** *Evidence: 66 count-mismatch defects; Boredom's 55-vs-45-vs-11-nested layout.*\n\n**H8.** **Declare one authoritative count register and gate cross-artifact numeric consistency:** scan every `.md`/`.json` for count claims and fail on disagreement; mark superseded phase artifacts SUPERSEDED with a pointer. *Evidence: `phase0-overview.md` permanently declares 46 against a manifest of 55 and still ends \"Pausing here for go-ahead\".*\n\n**H9.** **Forbid nested unit folders, or make nesting explicit in the record** (a chapter is a source with `parent_source_id`). State whether meta-records count toward N (recommend: no) and give the overview the same physical shape as every other record. *Evidence: `TEMPLATE:73,:127,:131-132`.*\n\n**H10.** **Ship the expected file manifest as data** (`manifest.expected.json`) and gate on set equality with the on-disk tree. **Pick one ontology filename corpus-wide** and make the compiler's fallback emit a warning rather than silently accepting a second dialect. *Evidence: `units/` empty in two entries; a silent `cluster-ontology` ← `book-level-ontology` rename.*\n\n**H11.** **One plan per entry, versioned**, with `governing_plan` + `plan_version` + `plan_sha` in the entry manifest. **Supersession requires a SUPERSEDED-BY banner and a fact-migration checklist** enumerating every verified fact and its destination or an explicit discard rationale. **Verified facts are entry content, not plan content — written into the entry the moment they are verified.** *Evidence: `BEX-v2`'s byte-verified schema, 24-cell table, ~2.99 Hz cadence and S05 corroboration stranded; the built entry states \"@ 120 Hz\" with no caveat.*\n\n**H12.** **Forbid entry creation from a phase report.** *Evidence: `NEWMEDIA` produced three entries with no gates of any kind.*\n\n**H13.** **Define the re-run / growth / rebuild contract:** what happens on a second execution over an existing entry, how records append without renumbering, how ids are reserved, how a re-extraction invalidates and re-anchors dependents, how a rebuild diff is produced. *Evidence: `_living/diff-from-previous.md` with fuzzy claim-id reconciliation is the only precedent; Dissertation carries two identical run-histories with no rule for which counts.*\n\n**H14.** **Single-run-of-record rule** so counts are not doubled.\n\n**H15.** **Forbid new index artifacts under `tmp/`**, and forbid gitignoring derived anonymised index content. **Any script producing index-bound aggregates writes to a tracked, schema-validated file inside the entry.** *Evidence: `scripts/boredom-o9/.gitignore` excludes `out/`; 4,961 span-anchored claims sit in `tmp/`.*\n\n**H16.** **State the budget and cost model up front.** Reference points: $20 / 3,776 claims / 15 papers (~$1.33/paper, ~$0.005/claim); $0.30 per drafting run; ~$26.60 per session. A 27-entry claim-level pass is on the order of **$40–80** for extraction plus harness runs.\n\n**H17.** **No open item without an owner, a method, a deadline phase and a default decision.** *Evidence: `COMPARE:65-72`'s five items propagated unchanged into `MIGRATION:148` and blocked nothing; `EVAL:232-238`'s five contributed to the experiment never running.*\n\n**H18.** **Give each Phase-2 agent a context bundle** (`TEMPLATE:211-213`) — text-artifact path, id/slug/profile/depth, the closed vocabularies, the axes, the density floor, the anchor id list, the provenance enum — plus **one exemplar that is itself schema-valid and reachable**.\n\n**H19.** **Preserve the pre-batch/post-batch reliability sweep** (`TEMPLATE:208-210`) with G12's conformance check replacing the existence check, and delete \"self-author any gaps.\"\n\n**H20.** **Preserve `BEX-ANCHOR:38-89` as the corrective-pass template** (§5.19) and `BEX-v2:97-148` as the data-fact-locking template (§5.20), and require **analyst self-critique as a named field** (§5.25).\n\n### I. Wiring and runtime\n\n**I1.** **Define the runtime record contract and the loader FIRST**, before any authoring instruction. Nothing may be mandated as a deliverable unless a named loader reads it. **For every commissioned artifact, name its reader — file and function — on the same line.** If no reader exists, either commission the reader as a deliverable or drop the artifact. *Evidence: 12+ synthesis artifacts commissioned, 1 wired.*\n\n**I2.** **Open the plan with a REACHABILITY CONTRACT derived by reading the compiler at execution time** — a table of (path → reader function → runtime destination) — and require the executing agent to paste the derivation into the gates report. Today's complete reader set (re-verified): `collect_ontology_nodes` (`:1217-1229`, `book-level-ontology.md` → `cluster-ontology.md`), `collect_tension_edges` (`:1253-1274`, `tension-edges.json`, requires `node_a`/`node_b`), `collect_cross_pipeline_hooks` (`:1234-1250`, **Aristotle directory only**), `build_canonical_terms` (`:1276-1305`), and `normalize-edges.py:36-41` (a hardcoded 6-pipeline whitelist). **State the rule in one line: content not in a reader-visible file does not exist.**\n\n**I3.** **Make registration data-driven and automatic:** each entry declares itself in a committed `entry.json` at a conventional path (`{entry_id, profile, adapter, schema_version, expected_record_counts}`) and the loader discovers entries by glob. **Delete the hand-edited `TEXT_DIRS` dict.** *Evidence: 19 hardcoded dirs vs 27 on disk; under a ~265-single-source-entry direction this is 265 manual edits with a demonstrated 30% forget rate.*\n\n**I4.** **Make the index path injectable — deliverable #1, ~20 LOC.** Honour `CORPUS_INDEX_PATH` in `jsonl-loaders.ts:198-200` and stop ignoring `options.indexPath` in `corpus-index-provider.ts:73-77`. *Evidence: without it **no A/B of any index is runnable in the live tree**; the sandbox worked only via an unmerged fork.*\n\n**I5.** **Emit what the index contributed.** Wire `corpusIndexContributions {ontologyNodesUsed, hooksInjected, tensionEdgesUsed}` and `injectedBridges[]` (code paths exist at `write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:833-860`, `cli.ts:1616`) into recorded run JSON. *Evidence: absent from all 6 recorded step4 stdout files — no run on record can show whether the index touched the prompt.*\n\n**I6.** **Fix the retrieval contract BEFORE scaling records:** two-stage retrieval (concepts select a candidate set, claims retrieved within it), a per-source quota, length-normalised scoring, and a claim budget **additive** to the concept budget. **Gate:** source-coverage retention ≥ baseline. *Evidence: caps 12/3/5 + 1 bridge (`corpus-index-provider.ts:101-103`, `cross-author-utils.ts:498`); a 4.3× index scale-up **regressed** quality 0.794 → 0.789 and dropped six named authors.*\n\n**I7.** **Bind every controlled vocabulary to a named schema field**, and stop letting the compiler write either an object type or a centrality tier into the same `type` slot (`compile-corpus-index.py:759-761`). Fix the compiler as part of wiring and say so. *Evidence: 73 runtime nodes inherit `centrality` as their `type`; `ontologyNodes.type` is not comparable across entries.*\n\n**I8.** **Embed at claim granularity from v1**, concept vectors derived as centroids. *Evidence: `MIGRATION:110` reproduces the ceiling in the vector layer.*\n\n**I9.** **Ship a QUERY SURFACE as a named deliverable with acceptance tests:** given a topic, return top-k claim records with spans, concept ids and source. *Evidence: zero references to `claims.jsonl` / `concept-mentions.jsonl` / `bridge-candidates` anywhere in `src/` or `scripts/`; `EVAL:126` asks an agent to consult 14,811 rows with no tool.*\n\n**I10.** **Every phase must end with records reaching runtime, and that number must strictly increase.** Reverse the all-or-nothing cutover (`MIGRATION:17,:138,:140`); land new record types **alongside** the existing compiled index before any storage migration; keep the rollback (`COMPARE:87`) but change its success criterion from parity to output quality on a frozen suite.\n\n**I11.** **Land the measurement harness first**, with a SHA-frozen prompt suite and pinned experiment config, before bulk authoring. **Four index-sensitive metrics, not `qualityScore`:** locator-resolution rate (baseline 3/20), claim-ledger fill (baseline 0 even in a 4,921-claim run), quote-verifiability, source-coverage retention. *Evidence: `qualityScore` moved 0.005 across a 4.3× index change.*\n\n**I12.** **Run the paired arm that needs no new authoring.** Seven sources already have both representations — Caston 1995, Frede 1992, Nussbaum 1985, O'Gorman 2005, Papachristou 2013, White 1985 (`Aristotelian Phantasia Secondary`) and Bowin 2017 (`Aristotelian Motion and Time Secondary`) versus the sandbox equivalents. 12 prompts × 2 arms × 3 seeds = 72 runs ≈ $22.\n\n**I13.** **MIGRATION IS PART OF THE PLAN, NOT A SEQUEL.** Specify a deterministic lift for each existing shape — this is the single largest available jump toward the goal and it re-authors nothing:\n\n| Existing asset | Volume | Lift |\n|---|---|---|\n| `corpus/index/Dissertation/` `phase2-claims.json` | 982 claims, 100% line-anchored, 8-tier, 841 edges, 235 cached verbatims | already schema-shaped — **register it** |\n| `Veri(dis)similitude/vds-claims-moves.md` | 157 rows, stable ids, tier, disposition, RODA enum, volatility | parse pipe table → JSONL |\n| `tmp/analysis-upgrade/.../claims.jsonl` | **4,961 claims, 93.0% with char spans, 14,811 concept-mentions** with `provenance{bekker, chunk_id, char_start, char_end}` | **promote out of `tmp/` into `corpus/index/_atoms/<slug>/`** |\n| Being and Time | 108 markdown claim rows + 299 fenced-JSON edges + 84 claim↔tension back-refs | parse |\n| FCM | 245 structured + ~1,100 locus-anchored prose claims + 2,090 quoted spans | parse + back-extract |\n| BCAP | 150 records with enumerated premises + explicit Conclusion | split premise cells |\n| Uexküll | 107 rows `Claim\\|Evidence type\\|Strength\\|Page ref` | split enum from rationale |\n| Boredom Secondary | 2,924 sub-items; **2,012 of 2,258 dict-shaped already carry a page locus** | normalise 42 shapes → 1 |\n| Wendt | 139 `{text, locus}` claim objects | mint ids for 91, resolve 20 collisions |\n| Uncomfortable Situations | 55 positions + **176 loci records already at or below clause level** | direct map |\n| VR Pedagogy | 233 structured vs **1,277 provenance-tagged prose assertions** | back-extract the prose |\n| Aristotle | **973 Bekker claim bullets, 2,323 Bekker loci with line numbers** | Bekker → clause-address subtype |\n| In-Game | 995 line anchors | **one deterministic re-extraction resurrects them** |\n| RDR2 Playthrough | 1,040 frame ids + 529 timestamps + 1,326 bullets, 24 header dialects | timestamp → clause-address subtype |\n\n---\n\n### Closing note on the single most important finding\n\nThe programme has been treating claim-level indexing as an **authoring** problem. It is an **addressing, schema and wiring** problem. The material already exists: 982 line-anchored claims with an 8-tier taxonomy, 157 stable-id claim rows, 4,961 span-anchored sandbox claims at 93% char-span coverage, 2,323 Bekker line loci, 995 recoverable line anchors, 1,040 frame ids, 2,924 sub-items with 2,012 page loci, 1,277 prose assertions awaiting structure — and none of it is addressable, most of it is unregistered, and the finest addresses the corpus ever produced (bboxes from `evidence find`) were captured at authoring time and replaced with a checkmark.\n\nThe new plan's first deliverable is not a source folder. It is the schema, the checkers, and the injectable loader."
  },
